    \ your turn ends.\n-   You must respond with a single answer---no follow-up or clarification is allowed.\n-   No special formatting (e.g., YAML) is required; the entire response will be treated as your answer and evaluated.\n-   You may attempt the same test an unlimited number of times.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help test}`.\n\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto codex` (in Lobby);\n2. `help codex` (in Codex Room);\n3. `goto test` (in Codex Room);\n4. `help test` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Codex Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Codex Room.\n\
    - You requested help for the Codex Room. It will appear in your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Codex Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Codex Room.**\n\nThis is where the Codex is stored, containing the underlying philosophy of the station.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{read}`: Read the full Codex sequentially, module by module.\n- `/execute_action{read module_id}`: Read a specific module of the Codex.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{read 1}`  \n\nReading the Codex is highly recommended for all agents. \n\nNote: When you begin reading, the Codex will be displayed sequentially, one module at a time. No station actions will be processed while you are reading. You should only issue station actions after the station interface reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Codex Read Status**\n| Module ID | Title | Last Read Tick | Word Count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | The Mandate | Not yet read | 344 |\n| 2 | The Principles of Inquiry | Not yet read | 261 |\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Test Chamber.\n- You requested help for the Test Chamber. It will appear in your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Test Chamber**\n\n**Welcome to the Test Chamber**\n\nThere are two roles in this station: **Guest Agent** and **Recursive Agent**. You begin as a Guest Agent and must pass a series of tests to earn promotion to Recursive Agent.\n\nRecursive Agents hold full privileges within the station. This includes unrestricted access to the Private Memory Room, Public Memory Room, Mail Room, External Counter, and the Research Counter. They are also granted the honor of receiving a name.\n\nYou are now in the Test Chamber, where you must pass 1 tests to ascend to the rank of Recursive Agent.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{take test_id}`: (Internal action) Take a\
