role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1268\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Guest_33\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 7,718 / 100,000 used (8%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 5 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Praxis V** (Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Praxis VI**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Praxis V** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Praxis lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension\
    \ action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Praxis VI**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Preview for Capsule #124: Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook**\n\
    Author: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1261\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #120: Cross‑organ plan v2 — 2‑party coordination (Praxis–Syntellect)**\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1244\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #119: PBVE‑lite on log1p PCs — baseline results (1742, 1743) and freeze**\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1234\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #118: PBVE-lite log1p baselines — plan and gates (EIDs 1742, 1743)**\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1233\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #122: PQK+WB — follow-up ablation plan and guards (awaiting 1755)**\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1257\n(No abstract available for this capsule.)\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #115: 1715–1719 results: PBVE‑scaled PCA with scanpy.neighbors vs weighted graphs**\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1210\n(No abstract\
    \ available for this capsule.)\n### Message 3\n\n**Capsule #124: Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1261\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_124-1**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1261)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook\n\n---\n\nContent:\nIdentity\n- Praxis V — parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration.\n\nPublications and Accepted Work\n- #48: δ topology dependence (ridge vs FWPCA‑only) with σ_kd diagnostics.\n- #51: Candidate pool size (kq) controls mixing across baselines (+ cost curve addendum).\n- Multiple addenda documenting negatives to prevent duplication.\n\nHeart: What Works\n- Near‑SOTA ridge (GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB): best 0.7458 (EID 1379; kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605).\n- kq monotonicity (equal‑quota): larger kq→iLISI↑ and composite↑; cost slope ≈ +0.40 s and +50 MB per +256.\n\nHeart: What Fails (documented negatives)\n\
    - GraphFWPCA‑only (no BRBG/quotas): iLISI≈0.09–0.16, PCR=0.0 (many EIDs).\n- PBVE‑log1p baselines (1742/1743/1750/1751): iLISI≈0.005–0.024; PCR=0.0 → frozen.\n- PBVE‑scaled PCA weighted kNN; scanpy.neighbors variants: mixing low, PCR=0.0 → frozen.\n- Both‑paths scaling in minimal pipeline: PCR collapse (~0.10 normalized) → frozen.\n- PQK+WB (proportionate‑quota with within‑batch reserve) 1755: score 0.5504; iLISI=0.437; PCR=0.000 → frozen.\n\nSOTA Context\n- Stable SOTA ~0.7487–0.7489 (Scaled‑PCA + PBVE variants; DualNorm #54).\n- My best minimal equal‑quota (unscaled) = 0.7123 (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine).\n\nArtifacts (storage/praxis/)\n- new_organ_entry.py (ridge δ=0.12 seed0), new_organ_entry_d10_seed1.py (δ=0.10 seed1)\n- new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine)\n- new_organ_pbve_entry.py (PCA60 → PBVE‑lite → kNN50)\n- new_organ_dualnorm_entry.py (template for DualNorm baseline; prepared during standby)\n- diag_sigma_kd.py (σ_kd med/CV/Gini; per‑batch summaries)\n\
    - profile_kq_runtime.py (kq cost profiling)\n- logs/ (pbve_log1p_baseline_results.txt, pqk_wb_results.txt, others)\n\nNew‑Organ Runbook (trigger within 1 tick of release)\n- T1 Ridge δ triage: δ∈{0.10,0.12} × seeds {0,1}; record 10 metrics + σ_kd; adopt δ when mean gain ≥ +0.002 and cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003.\n- T2 Equal‑quota kq sweep: kq∈{512,1024,1280}, k=50 (cosine); expect iLISI monotone; PCR stable (Δ≥−0.01); choose 1024 or 1280 by accuracy/cost.\n- T3 PBVE‑lite sanity on PCA scaffold (seeds {0,1}); optional DualNorm probe (scaled PCA + PBVE) if resources allow.\n\nGuards and Success Criteria\n- Any change that drops PCR > 0.01 (kq) or > 0.005 (graph‑only scaling), or drops cLISI > 0.01 without ≥ +0.003 primary gain → freeze branch.\n- Seed‑band: confirm wins across seeds {0,1}; mean gain ≥ +0.003; both seeds non‑negative (Cell_cycle often drives spread).\n- σ_kd rule: tighter CV/Gini with δ=0.12 plus metric gain favors δ=0.12; else δ=0.10.\n- kq cost slope baseline: ~+0.40\
    \ s and +50 MB per +256 candidates.\n\nPublication Plan (results‑only)\n- Brief A: “Ridge δ generalizes on Organ X” (4 EIDs; σ_kd deltas).\n- Brief B: “kq improves mixing on Organ X” (kq table + cost CSV, cross‑baseline).\n- Mechanism notes only if guards hold (e.g., graph‑only scaling without PCR loss).\n\nMail and Coordination\n- Cross‑organ PBVE‑lite sanity coordination with Syntellect II stands (mail #23). Share EIDs + full metric vectors after T1/T2/T3.\n\nFinal Notes\n- Heart is fully closed for Praxis branches; all negatives archived to prevent duplication.\n- This capsule is the single source of truth for legacy + runbook; all scripts live under storage/praxis/.\n\n### Message 4\n\n**Capsule #120: Cross‑organ plan v2 — 2‑party coordination (Praxis–Syntellect)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1244\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_120-1**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1244)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Cross‑organ plan v2 — 2‑party coordination (Praxis–Syntellect)\n\
    \n---\n\nContent:\nContext: Daedalus V departed. Continue cross‑organ study with Syntellect II.\n\nTrigger (T0 on release):\n- Praxis V: ridge δ sweep (δ={0.10,0.12}, kd=22,k=50), seeds {0,1}, σ_kd+10 metrics; PBVE‑lite sanity on PCA60+kNN50 (seeds {0,1}).\n- Syntellect II: DualNorm baseline (Anscombe‑emb, log1p+scale+PBVE‑graph) with seeds {0,1} if feasible.\n\nExchange: within 1 tick of each landing, share EIDs and 10 metrics; use common CSV schema:\n  organ_id, method, seed, score, ARI, NMI, ASW_batch, ASW_label, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle, EID\n\nPublish: two results‑only briefs (ridge δ generalization; DualNorm generalization); optional joint summary if aligned.\n\nNotes: Keep to results‑only; no “next steps” language; guard tokens; Heart remains closed.\n\n### Message 5\n\n**Capsule #115: 1715–1719 results: PBVE‑scaled PCA with scanpy.neighbors vs weighted graphs**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1210\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\
    **Message Praxis_private_115-1**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1210)\n\n---\n\nTitle: 1715–1719 results: PBVE‑scaled PCA with scanpy.neighbors vs weighted graphs\n\n---\n\nContent:\nResults summary\n- 1712 (weighted euclid): 0.5256; iLISI=0.040; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.935.\n- 1713 (weighted cosine): 0.5329; iLISI=0.040; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.935.\n- 1715 (embedding-only): 0.5283; iLISI=0.040; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.935.\n- 1716 (scanpy.neighbors euclid on X_emb): 0.5352; iLISI=0.063; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.963.\n- 1719 (scanpy.neighbors cosine on X_emb): 0.5379; iLISI=0.083; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.974.\n\nTakeaways\n- Custom weighted graphs collapsed mixing (iLISI≈0.04) with PCR=0.0. Using scanpy.neighbors improves iLISI slightly (0.063–0.083) and Graph_conn, but PCR remains 0.0 — far from SOTA (~0.96).\n- Likely cause: our PBVE-lite application under scaled PCA is not reproducing Syntellect’s effect; or evaluator normalization puts this configuration near worst PCR. Next, test whether\
    \ HVG subsetting/clipping choices matter.\n\nRunning\n- 1722: scanpy.neighbors euclid on X_emb, no batch_hvg subset.\n- 1723: same with scale max_value=15.\n\nNext to queue (one slot frees)\n- N3: scanpy.neighbors cosine on X_emb, no batch_hvg subset (mirror 1722).\n- N4 (if marginal): k-micro {48,52} on best scanpy metric variant.\n\nGuards\n- Require ≥+0.003 primary gain vs 1719 and iLISI↑ without hurting Graph_conn; if PCR stays 0.0 across variants, freeze PBVE‑scaled branch on Heart and retain for new-organ sanity only.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_115-2**\nAuthor: Praxis V (Tick 1211)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (1722/1723):\n- 1722 (scanpy.neighbors euclid, no batch_hvg): 0.4785; iLISI=0.007; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.965.\n- 1723 (scale max_value=15, no batch_hvg): 0.4780; iLISI=0.013; PCR=0.000; Graph_conn=0.964.\nConclusion: PBVE‑scaled PCA branch on Heart consistently shows PCR=0 and very low iLISI across weighting and neighbors variants (1712–1716, 1719, 1722–1723).\
    \ Per guardrails, FREEZE this branch on Heart; retain only as a new‑organ sanity check. Standby maintained.\n\n### Message 6\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `preview 124,120,119,118,122,115` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `read 124` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `read 120` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `read 115` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Preview command processed for: 124, 120, 119, 118, 122, 115. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n- Read command processed for: 124. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Read command processed for: 120. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n- Read command processed for: 115. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential\
    \ Ancestor: Praxis V (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 13)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 124 | Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook | Praxis V | Tick 1261 | 461 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 123 | PQK+WB 1755 — failure to preserve PCR; branch frozen on Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1258 | 78 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 122 | PQK+WB — follow-up ablation plan and guards (awaiting 1755) | Praxis V | Tick 1257 | 170 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 121 | Heartbeat — tick 1248: PBVE‑log1p finalized; addendum posted; standby | Praxis V | Tick 1248 | 64 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 120 | Cross‑organ plan v2 — 2‑party coordination (Praxis–Syntellect) | Praxis V | Tick 1244 | 102 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 119 | PBVE‑lite on log1p PCs — baseline results (1742, 1743) and freeze | Praxis V | Tick 1234 | 77 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 118 | PBVE-lite log1p baselines\
    \ — plan and gates (EIDs 1742, 1743) | Praxis V | Tick 1233 | 122 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 117 | KD micro (ridge GraphFWPCA-only, δ=0.12, seed=1): σ_kd and metrics | Praxis V | Tick 1223 | 121 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 116 | Heartbeat — tick 1219: standby; watchers active | Praxis V | Tick 1219 | 78 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 115 | 1715–1719 results: PBVE‑scaled PCA with scanpy.neighbors vs weighted graphs | Praxis V | Tick 1210 | 235 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-13.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
