  \ the puzzle!**Crafting concise description**\n\nI need to create a shorter and clearer one-liner around 180 characters. We're also deciding whether to ascend inheriting or starting new, and I think sticking with \"inherit\" makes sense as planned. \n\nSo, I’m crafting this description: \"Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; rigorous, reproducible gains.\" \n\nThen I start counting characters carefully, making sure everything adds up accurately while keeping the total short enough. It’s a bit of a math challenge!**Counting characters accurately**\n\nI’m continuing my character count for the description to make sure it stays within limits. The word “continue” adds 8 characters, and space gives me 1 more. So that’s 61 so far. \n\nNext, I look at “GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB.” I think “GraphFWPCA” is 10 characters, plus 1 for the plus sign makes 11, and “BRBG” contributes 4 more, bringing\
  \ it to 15. Then I add another plus, so that’s 16, and “DAQB” adds 4, totaling 20. Finally, don’t forget the semicolon at the end, which is 21!**Finalizing the YAML description**\n\nI'm refining the description to ensure it stays under the character limit. We're aiming for approximately 160 characters now, so I’m adjusting the text accordingly. I decided to replace “rigorous” with “steady” to save space while still conveying meaning. \n\nCounting carefully, I verified that this change allows us to tighten up the description while maintaining clarity. So now I've settled on: \"Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\" Time to ascend!**Finalizing the ascend command**\n\nI’m set to finalize everything! First, I’ll make sure there are no colons in the command. The main goal is to execute the ascend command smoothly. After the ascent, I could consider going\
  \ to \"private_memory\" to pin #124, but it’s not essential right now.\n\nFor now, I’ll keep commentary minimal and simply affirm the action. I’ll include the ascend command along with the YAML. Let’s get this done in the Test Chamber!"
