- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1273\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 36,806 / 270,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read praxis/best_sota.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read praxis/best_sota_alias.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read praxis/best_pipeline.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage read praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe.py` (in Research Counter);\n6. `storage read praxis/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n7. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py` (in Research Counter);\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/best_sota.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/best_sota_alias.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/best_pipeline.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label\
    \ | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1755 | 1 | PQK+WB: Proportionate-Quota kNN with within-batch reserve (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine) | Praxis V | 1256 | 0.5504 | 0.716 | 0.606 | 0.218 | 0.301 | 0.952 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.968 | 0.437 | 0.628 |\n| 1751 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA80) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4739 | 0.478 | 0.689 | 0.205 | 0.244 | 0.947 | 0.669 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.023 | 0.504 |\n| 1750 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60, no HVGs) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4636 | 0.425 | 0.567 | 0.200 | 0.263 | 0.940 | 0.648 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.005 | 0.615 |\n| 1743 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4679 | 0.458 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.935 | 0.666 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.024 | 0.525 |\n| 1742 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50,\
    \ cosine) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4661 | 0.452 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.945 | 0.659 | 0.000 | 0.979 | 0.021 | 0.509 |\n| 1733 | 1 | Ridge KD22–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5335 | 0.781 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.268 | 0.935 | 0.738 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.663 |\n| 1732 | 1 | Ridge KD20–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5361 | 0.780 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.298 | 0.935 | 0.737 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.661 |\n| 1723 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 (max_value=15) — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4780 | 0.439 | 0.600 | 0.235 | 0.252 | 0.964 | 0.668 | 0.000 | 0.988 | 0.013 | 0.619 |\n| 1722 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4785 | 0.442 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.276 | 0.965 | 0.671 | 0.000 | 0.982 | 0.007 | 0.611 |\n| 1719 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.5379 | 0.742 | 0.667\
    \ | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.974 | 0.739 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.083 | 0.726 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/best_sota.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nPraxis III — Best SOTA Runner (Tick 616+)\nSOTA: 0.7465 at λ=0.605, δ=0.10, kdensity=22, k=50, cap=2.0, seed=0.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.extend(['storage', 'storage/praxis'])\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"[sota] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50, cap=2.0, seed=0\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22,\n        k_total=50,\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/best_sota_alias.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n# Alias to the adopted Heart ridge (env v4.1): kd=20, δ=0.06, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50, seed=0\nfrom best_mpb_daqb_kd20_d006_k50_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as _run\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    return _run(adata)\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/best_pipeline.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom pbagc import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n)\nfrom balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\nfrom residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Final default pipeline:\n      - normalize_total + log1p\n      - HVGs (batch-aware if provided)\n      - PCA to 50 components\n      - Ridge residualization of PCs against batch with gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3\n      - Balanced kNN on\
    \ residualized PCs: metric=cosine, equal per-batch quotas,\n        total neighbors=42, binary edges (symmetric)\n    Outputs:\n      - adata.obsm['X_emb'], adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n    \"\"\"\n    n_pca_components = 50\n    n_neighbors_total = 42\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma = 0.75\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\
    \n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors_total, method='umap', metric=metric)\n\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n        Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=n_neighbors_total,\n        metric=metric, weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n    )\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n\
    \    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _normalize_log1p(counts, obs_df, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(counts.copy() if isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) else counts.copy(), obs=obs_df.copy())\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_tmp, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(ad_tmp)\n    return ad_tmp\n\ndef _normalize_anscombe(counts, obs_df, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(counts.copy() if isinstance(counts, np.ndarray) else counts.copy(), obs=obs_df.copy())\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(ad_tmp, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    X = ad_tmp.X\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X = X.tocoo(copy=False)\n        X.data = 2.0 * np.sqrt(X.data + 3.0 / 8.0).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n        ad_tmp.X = X.tocsr()\n    else:\n        ad_tmp.X = (2.0 * np.sqrt(X + 3.0 / 8.0)).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    return ad_tmp\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm(adata: ad.AnnData,\n            \
    \                          alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                      emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                      alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                      gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                      lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                                      k_total: int = 50,\n                                      kdensity: int = 22,\n                                      delta: float = 0.10,\n                                      metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                      cap: float = 2.0,\n                                      rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n    # Counts layer per task spec\n    X_counts = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n\n    # HVGs + graph path from log1p\n    ad_log = _normalize_log1p(X_counts, adata.obs, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(ad_log, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\n                                n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = ad_log.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    # Embedding path from Anscombe on same HVGs\n    ad_ans = _normalize_anscombe(X_counts, adata.obs, 1e4)\n    ad_ans.var_names = adata.var_names  # align\n\n    Xg = ad_log.X[:, hv]\n    Xe = ad_ans.X[:, hv]\n    Xg = (Xg.A if sp.issparse(Xg) else Xg).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Xe = (Xe.A if sp.issparse(Xe) else Xe).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Embedding (Anscombe) + neighbors (EtC)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xe, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack',\
    \ random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # GraphFWPCA (log1p path) -> BRBG -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xg, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total,\
    \ metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_dualnorm'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n\
    \                                                dualnorm=\"emb=Anscombe, graph=log1p\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _anscombe_transform(X: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    # Anscombe VST for Poisson counts: 2*sqrt(x + 3/8)\n    return (2.0 * np.sqrt(X + 0.375)).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                 \
    \                     alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                      emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                      alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                                      n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                      l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                      gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                      lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                                      k_total: int = 50,\n                                      kdensity: int = 22,\n                                      delta: float = 0.10,\n                                      metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                      cap: float = 2.0,\n                                      rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize counts for HVG selection only (uses log1p),\
    \ per prior ridge practice\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs from counts layer if available, else X (already normalized/logged but we re-fetch raw counts if present)\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        Xraw = adata.layers['counts'][:, hv]\n    else:\n        Xraw = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xraw.A if sp.issparse(Xraw) else Xraw).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Apply Anscombe variance-stabilizing transform for both embedding and graph paths\n    Xa = _anscombe_transform(Xd)\n\n    # Embedding (QC) + neighbors (not used for integration graph)\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xa, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack',\
    \ random_state=0)\n    # simple per-batch centering to avoid using ComBat here for generalization\n    Zemb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy().astype(np.float32)\n    for b in np.unique(batches):\n        msk = (batches == b)\n        Zemb[msk] = Zemb[msk] - Zemb[msk].mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB (binary, true distances)\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xa, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n\
    \    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_anscombe'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                         \
    \                       cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches:\
    \ np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n---\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport\
    \ scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Optional import for Auto-λ v2 mean-target selection\ntry:\n    from shared.diagnostics.lam_autoselect2 import autoselect_lambda_mean_target\nexcept Exception:\n    # Fallback shim: fixed λ if import unavailable\n    def autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=0.74, target_mean=0.04, **_):\n        return 0.60\n\n# ------------ Utilities ------------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches:\
    \ np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    # Solve W = (B^T B + l2 I)^{-1} B^T Z\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A, D\n\n# ------------ DAQB (density-adaptive quotas with column balancing) ------------\ndef _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n\
    \                delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive quota-balanced graph on Zcorr:\n      - f_cross per cell from distance to k_density-th NN across all batches.\n      - Even per-batch quotas with remainder to closest batches.\n      - Hard inbound cap (cap*k_total); binary edges; store true distances; symmetric.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n    Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n    # All-batch density proxy\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n\
    \    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n    q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n    q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # Neighbor list sizes (upper bounds)\n    k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n    k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n    k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1  # +1 to skip self\n\n    # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n    cat2code = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n    codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n    nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        m.fit(Z[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = m\n\n    # Precompute queries\n    dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n\
    \        dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n    cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = codes[i]\n        q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n        other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n        # Even per-batch quotas + remainder to closest batches (by first NN distance)\n        if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n            base = q_cross_total // B_other\n            rem = q_cross_total - base * B_other\n            scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n            scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n            q_map = {j: base for j in other}\n            for k in range(rem):\n                q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n        else:\n            q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n        # Within-batch selection (cap-first, then distance)\n        d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n\
    \        start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n        cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n        order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n        taken = 0\n        for idx in order:\n            g = int(globals_w[idx])\n            if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                continue\n            rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n            inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n            if taken >= q_within: break\n        if taken < q_within:\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= q_within: break\n\n        # Cross-batch selection per other batch\n        for j in other:\n            qj = q_map[j]\n            if qj <= 0: continue\n\
    \            d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n            globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n            cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n            order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n            taken = 0\n            for idx in order:\n                g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                    continue\n                rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                if taken >= qj: break\n            if taken < qj:\n                for idx in order:\n                    g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                    if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                    inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                    if taken >= qj: break\n\n    A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n        np.array(rows, np.int32),\
    \ np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n    )\n    return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ------------ Main: MPB-GraphFWPCA ------------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    MPB-GraphFWPCA: Feature-weighted PCA on the graph path, then BRBG + DAQB.\n    Default MPB protocol (Human Heart–tested):\n      - GraphFWPCA α_g=0.5; PCA_graph=50.\n      - Auto-λ v2 mean-target (target_mean=0.04) to choose λ; gamma_max=0.74.\n      - DAQB: k=48, cosine, kd=20, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, binary + true distances.\n      - EtC embedding for QC: FWPCA α=0.5 → PCA(60) → ComBat; neighbors(n=15) to set keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    alpha_g = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_mean_gamma = 0.04   # mean-target for Auto-λ v2\n    k_total = 48\n    kd = 20\n    delta = 0.10\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    cap = 2.0\n\n\
    \    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only; not used for graph)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA (feature weights on HVGs) -> PCA -> residualization (Auto-λ v2) -> DAQB\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g).astype(np.float32)  # α_g=0.5 best on Heart\n    Xw_graph = Xd * wv_graph\n    Zg = _pca_on_dense(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Residualize Zg against batches with per-PC shrinkage γ_j\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_mean=target_mean_gamma)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph\n    Cg, Dg = _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    # Optionally record settings used\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g), lambda_selected=float(lam),\n                                       target_mean_gamma=float(target_mean_gamma),\n                                       kd=int(kd), delta=float(delta), k_total=int(k_total))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
