  \ a Private Memory Capsule to record results. I’ll need to go to private_memory to create it, but I want to be careful about spending too many tokens writing long content now. It might be better to wait for the results to come in.**Assessing current metrics**\n\nEach station tick represents a turn for each agent, and our next response is immediate, though we might not have results yet. Sometimes the system processes quickly, so we can use /execute_action{rank score} to see our standing on the leaderboard. I think it only shows evaluations from the Research Counter, but sorting might highlight the top performers as well. \n\nSince we're running two in parallel, we can't submit more, but we could write code modifications for storage. Yet, our code is already parameterized, so that might not be necessary. I should also check system storages for metrics and set further meta information.**Considering communication options**\n\nI’m thinking about sending a high-level message in the Mail Room\
  \ to Syntellect II. The Common Room and Public Memory require maturity, but the Mail Room is accessible to all Recursive Agents. \n\nWhile direct collaboration is prohibited, high-level communication is encouraged, so I could share EIDs and metrics with Syntellect II. However, it might not be necessary since we're currently in an isolation period due to not achieving maturity (13 ticks). This isolation limits access to certain rooms but allows limited mail communication. As a recursive agent, I have unrestricted access to some rooms like Private Memory and the Research Counter.**Navigating the isolation period**\n\nDuring the Isolation Period, access to certain rooms like the Archive, Public Memory, and Common Room is restricted, but I can still use the Mail Room for high-level communication. Sharing EIDs and metrics is allowed, but I should avoid direct collaboration. \n\nI'll record results quickly in Private Memory and summarize them in a capsule titled \"New Organ Heart: MPB vs EQ-Quota\
  \ results.\" Meanwhile, I'll wait for results from tests 1770 and 1771, and set watchers if needed. I’ll issue commands for submissions and prepare to track performance while keeping my actions concise. Let's implement the necessary actions while maintaining clarity throughout!"
