    \ has been set.\n- Evaluation 'MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.102 (DAQB)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1774.\n- Evaluation 'MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 (DAQB)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1775.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1775 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1279 |\n| 1774 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.102 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1279 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1775 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k48 δ0.10 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1279 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1774 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.102 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1279 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1773 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.12 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1277 | 0.7398 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.310 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.789 |\n| 1772 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override λ0.605 kd22 k50 δ0.10 (DAQB) | Praxis VI | 1277 | 0.7392 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.304 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 1770 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB (Anscombe) kd=22 delta=0.12 k=50 | Praxis VI | 1275 | 0.6637 | 0.587 | 0.385 | 0.073 | 0.459 | 0.995 | 0.647 | 1.000 | 0.956 | 0.951 | 0.583 |\n| 1771 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB (Anscombe) kd=22 delta=0.10 k=50 | Praxis VI | 1275 | 0.6686 | 0.577 | 0.385 | 0.073 | 0.513 | 0.994 | 0.643 | 1.000 | 0.957 | 0.963 | 0.581 |\n| 1769 | 1 | Equal-Quota Ridge-Residualized\
    \ PCA graph (k=50, kq=1280, cosine) | Praxis VI | 1274 | 0.5893 | 0.760 | 0.606 | 0.218 | 0.301 | 0.945 | 0.701 | 0.000 | 0.969 | 0.768 | 0.626 |\n| 1768 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA + DAQB (shared baseline, Auto-λ v2, k=48 cosine) | Praxis VI | 1273 | 0.7358 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.789 |\n| 1755 | 1 | PQK+WB: Proportionate-Quota kNN with within-batch reserve (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine) | Praxis V | 1256 | 0.5504 | 0.716 | 0.606 | 0.218 | 0.301 | 0.952 | 0.679 | 0.000 | 0.968 | 0.437 | 0.628 |\n| 1750 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60, no HVGs) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4636 | 0.425 | 0.567 | 0.200 | 0.263 | 0.940 | 0.648 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.005 | 0.615 |\n| 1751 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA80) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1245 | 0.4739 | 0.478 | 0.689 | 0.205 | 0.244 | 0.947 | 0.669 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.023 | 0.504 |\n| 1743 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors\
    \ (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4679 | 0.458 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.935 | 0.666 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.024 | 0.525 |\n| 1742 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4661 | 0.452 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.945 | 0.659 | 0.000 | 0.979 | 0.021 | 0.509 |\n| 1732 | 1 | Ridge KD20–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5361 | 0.780 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.298 | 0.935 | 0.737 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.661 |\n| 1733 | 1 | Ridge KD22–K50 δ=0.12 (seed=1) — σ_kd logging | Praxis V | 1221 | 0.5335 | 0.781 | 0.668 | 0.205 | 0.268 | 0.935 | 0.738 | 0.000 | 0.915 | 0.163 | 0.663 |\n| 1719 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.5379 | 0.742 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.974 | 0.739 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.083 | 0.726 |\n| 1722 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4785 | 0.442 | 0.596 | 0.236 |\
    \ 0.276 | 0.965 | 0.671 | 0.000 | 0.982 | 0.007 | 0.611 |\n| 1723 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 (max_value=15) — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4780 | 0.439 | 0.600 | 0.235 | 0.252 | 0.964 | 0.668 | 0.000 | 0.988 | 0.013 | 0.619 |\n| 1715 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — Embedding only (no graph) | Praxis V | 1207 | 0.5283 | 0.737 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.935 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.040 | 0.725 |\n| 1716 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — sc.pp.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1207 | 0.5352 | 0.752 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.963 | 0.744 | 0.000 | 0.983 | 0.063 | 0.724 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport\
    \ scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override:\
    \ float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                        \
    \        k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
