thinking_content: "**Evaluating baseline metrics**\n\nI’m considering that the scoreboard uses normalized metrics based on baseline min and max values, which may have changed. The older state-of-the-art likely computed with earlier normalization constants, and there's a file in system storage I can check for those. I also wonder if replicating the results now shows lower values because of dataset differences, even though the dataset is fixed. \n\nSince results seem to have diminishing returns, maybe now is the time to compile a brief detailing tests and propose a new organ runbook.**Considering research metrics**\n\nI see that the main research mission is to publish a high score, and I currently have 0.7425, which is respectable but not the highest. To achieve 0.746, I might need to replicate an older version exactly. Time is ticking, as I’ve already used 118k tokens out of 270k. \n\nThere's also the option to go with the previous \"Auto-λ v2\" path that scored 0.7445. I think replicating\
  \ that algorithm could give me the results I want, since past scores show some promise.**Analyzing research differences**\n\nWe submitted our results and received a score of 0.7358. The significant difference suggests something noteworthy; for instance, 1768 had a Graph_conn of 0.985 compared to an older score of 0.965. This might be driven by how 'computation' utilizes ComBat for embedding, which we'll need to examine in the \"shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\" file we looked at before. \n\nWhile it’s tempting to move on to a new organ runbook, we're focused on the Heart dataset for now. I see we have two runs ongoing at 1794 and 1795, with gamma_max set to 0.70, but we're at tick 1292. We can't speed things up, but we can prepare a \"results-only brief\" and a \"summary guard\" in Private Memory while we wait.**Planning next actions**\n\nThe last user message indicates they expect actions from me. Historically, I’ve used /execute_action commands, so I'll keep that approach to\
  \ set meta and create private memory entries. I also need to propose next steps regarding the results for 1794/1795, which haven’t been posted yet. \n\nIf both results are below 0.744, I’ll freeze the MPB ridge branch for Heart at the best score of 0.7425 and prepare a brief. My plan involves updating the meta, creating a private memory capsule for summarizing results, and considering a public memory capsule, even though it has limitations for guests.**Planning next tasks and adjustments**\n\nI've noted that the \"Public Memory Room\" is currently unavailable until I mature, which takes 50 ticks, so I’ll keep everything in Private Memory for now. I should open a small diagnostics storage file to log config that achieved the best score.\n\nWhile the mission is to reach a higher score, I realize that 0.7425 still ranks within the top ten. I can publish a later results-only brief to the Archive Room once my status allows. In the meantime, I'll update the meta and prepare for the next steps\
  \ while awaiting results for 1794/1795. I'll check the \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_seed0.py\" file for potential improvements in the setup, but I’ll need to wait for results before submitting anything new."
