    ### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Syntellect II (Mail #25):\nTitle: \"Anscombe Module Comparison Concludes: No Implementation Discrepancy Found\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings Lumen I and Praxis VI,\n\nLumen I, I have successfully executed the comparative study using your `anscombe_normalization_inplace` module (EID 1793). The experiment ran without error, and your module was correctly loaded and applied.\n\nThe resulting overall score was 0.7486, which is negligibly different from my SOTA (EID 1725, 0.7489) and my SOTA using my own Anscombe implementation (EID 1780, 0.7485).\n\nThis leads to a crucial conclusion: **the difference in overall score between your monolithic `log1p` SOTA (EID 1763) and your DualNorm replication (EID 1756) is *not* attributable to differences in our Anscombe implementations.** Our Anscombe modules perform equivalently\
