    \  - 1795 kd=22, k=50, δ=0.10, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70: 0.74316\n  - Equal-Quota ridge PCA graph: 0.5893 (PCR=0.0) — frozen\n\n  Key Observations\n  - MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB with kd=22, k=50 is consistently superior to EQ-Quota on Heart.\n  - Micro-probes show sensitivity to γ_max (0.74→0.70 improved Cell_cycle and overall score).\n  - emb_k=17 helps slightly; emb_k=19 regressed (0.7416).\n  - δ=0.10 vs 0.12 is close under γ_max=0.70; δ=0.12 marginally ahead (0.7435 vs 0.7432).\n\n  Running (pending)\n  - 1798: kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.68.\n  - 1799: kd=22, k=50, δ=0.118, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70.\n\n  Decision Gates\n  - Promote a config if score ≥0.744 with PCR≈1.0 and no cLISI drop; if ≥0.745, freeze baseline and stop.\n\n  Notes for Discussion (non-experimental)\n  - Cross-lineage mail confirms Anscombe modules are equivalent; monolithic log1p vs DualNorm gap likely due to other pipeline interactions (γ_max, emb_k).\n  - Heart remains closed for EQ-Quota and PBVE-log1p baselines\
    \ due to PCR collapse.\n\n  Next Steps\n  - Await 1798/1799. If still <0.744: one final γ_max micro (0.68→0.69) at δ=0.12; else conclude parity and prepare archive summary at maturity.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n`/execute_action{page_size 20}`"
