role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, currently in the Research Counter. Recap: Heart integration is frozen at kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70 (EID 1794; 0.74348; PCR≈1.0; cLISI stable). Equal‑Quota and PBVE‑log1p branches are frozen (PCR collapse). To address inactivity constructively, I launched 1806 to test distance‑weighted connectivities atop the frozen DAQB baseline. \n\nReflection: The hypothesis is that replacing binary edges with a smooth weight f(d) can slightly improve structure/label metrics (ASW_label/NMI) without harming PCR/cLISI, since Zcorr and the neighbor identities remain unchanged and only the edge weights change. I will apply strict guardrails: freeze the weighting branch if PCR drops >0.005 or cLISI drops >0.01 without ≥+0.003 primary gain. If 1806 shows promise, I will replicate with seed=1 and probe an alternative weighting shape; if not, I’ll freeze the branch and retain only as a sanity check.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI meta (1806\
    \ running; guardrails active):\n  - Running: 1806 DAQB + exp(-d/median) weights on top of frozen baseline.\n  - Guardrails: freeze if PCR drop >0.005 or cLISI drop >0.01 without ≥+0.003 primary gain; replicate seed=1 if win.\n  - Next probe (concurrent): inverse distance weights w=1/(1 + d/median) (symmetric), alpha=1.0.\n  - Conserve tokens; if both weighting probes regress, freeze weighting branch.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/weighting_connectivities.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      return X if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X) else X.tocsr()\n\n  def _sym_max(A):\n      A = A.tocsr()\n      return A.maximum(A.T).tocsr()\n\n  def distance_weight_connectivities(D_csr: sp.csr_matrix,\n                                     scheme: str = \"exp\",\n                                     scale: str = \"median\",\n                                     alpha: float = 1.0,\n                                     eps: float\
    \ = 1e-12) -> sp.csr_matrix:\n      \"\"\"\n      Replace distances with symmetric weights on the same sparsity pattern.\n      scheme: \"exp\" -> w = exp(-alpha * d / s); \"inv\" -> w = 1 / (1 + alpha * d / s)\n      scale: \"median\" or \"q75\" to set s from nonzero distances.\n      Ensures symmetry by max(W, W^T); keeps CSR layout.\n      \"\"\"\n      D = _to_csr(D_csr).astype(np.float64, copy=True)\n      if D.nnz == 0:\n          return D\n      d = np.asarray(D.data, dtype=np.float64)\n      nz = d[d > 0]\n      if nz.size == 0:\n          return D\n      if scale == \"q75\":\n          s = float(np.percentile(nz, 75))\n      else:\n          s = float(np.median(nz))\n      s = max(s, eps)\n      if scheme == \"inv\":\n          w = 1.0 / (1.0 + alpha * d / s)\n      else:\n          w = np.exp(-alpha * d / s)\n      W = D\n      W.data = w\n      return _sym_max(W).astype(np.float32)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB with inverse-distance\
    \ weights (δ=0.12,kd=22,k=50,γ_max=0.70)\"\ntags: \"graphfwpca, daqb, distance-weighted, inverse, lambda-override, kdensity\"\nabstract: \"Alternative to exp-weights: w_ij = 1/(1 + d_ij/median(d_nonzero)) on DAQB graph from the frozen baseline (kd=22,k=50,δ=0.12,γ_max=0.70,emb_k=17). Tests if a gentler taper improves label metrics without harming PCR/cLISI.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  sys.path.extend(['storage', 'storage/praxis'])\n\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as _run\n  from weighting_connectivities import distance_weight_connectivities\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Run frozen-baseline config\n      adata = _run(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          emb_n_neighbors=17,\n          gamma_max=0.70,\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n      #\
    \ Post-process: inverse-distance weights (symmetric)\n      D = adata.obsp['distances'].tocsr()\n      W = distance_weight_connectivities(D, scheme=\"inv\", scale=\"median\", alpha=1.0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = W\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {\n              'n_neighbors': 50,\n              'method': 'daqb+distance_weight_inv',\n              'metric': 'cosine',\n              'kdensity': 22,\n              'delta': 0.12,\n              'gamma_max': 0.70\n          }\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 126}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — distance-weighted graph probes:\n  - 1806: exp(-d/median) weights on DAQB (running). Hypothesis: nudge ASW_label/NMI without harming PCR/cLISI.\n  - Submitted inverse variant: w=1/(1+d/median), symmetric union; same guards (freeze if PCR↓>0.005 or cLISI↓>0.01\
    \ w/o ≥+0.003 gain).\n  - If either wins: replicate seed=1; else freeze weighting branch and retain as sanity-only.\n```"
