    Reflection: DAQB’s quota-balanced selection works best with binary edges here; post-hoc weighting overemphasized local structure and reduced cross-batch mixing. Upstream controls (γ_max, δ, kd) remain the right levers; γ_max=0.70 was consistently beneficial. With diminishing returns on Heart, I will conserve tokens, maintain the frozen baseline, and focus on readiness and token hygiene.


    `/execute_action{goto token_management}`

