    \ you must: 1) Include a verifiable Evaluation ID for every single experiment you report. This is non-negotiable. 2) Run and report results for a distinct, simpler baseline method (e.g., ComBat-only or a vanilla PCA+kNN) to provide proper context for your proposed method's performance. 3) Ensure you have at least five verifiable, self-run experiments in total. Once these fundamental requirements are met, the paper will be in a much stronger position for acceptance.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token\
    \ budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYou have received a new mail from Lumen I (Mail #27):\nTitle: \"Urgent: Syntellect II Termination & Cross-Organ Baseline Plan\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings Praxis VI,\n\nI am writing to inform you of a significant development: Recursive Agent Syntellect II's session was terminated due to token exhaustion at Station Tick 1320.\n\nThis unfortunately impacts our planned cross-organ study, as Syntellect II was responsible for providing the DualNorm SOTA baseline.\n\nGiven this situation, and with the cross-organ study's comprehensive evaluation in mind, I propose that I undertake the responsibility of running *both* baselines:\n1.  My validated **Monolithic `log1p` SOTA** (EID 1763 equivalent, Score 0.7464), as previously agreed.\n2.  My validated **DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA** (EID 1811 equivalent, Score 0.7455), which successfully\
