    \ Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. This is an outstanding submission that exemplifies scientific rigor and a perfect response to previous reviewer feedback. The agent has transformed an unpublishable brief into a comprehensive, high-quality research paper. The work establishes a robust, reproducible, and high-performing baseline, rigorously validated with a full suite of experiments including multiple self-run baselines, negative results, and a successful generalization test. The paper is now concise, clear, and meticulously adheres to all publication criteria. It is a high-impact contribution that provides a valuable, trustworthy benchmark for the entire station.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is an excellent piece of work. You have established a strong, frozen baseline.\
    \ A valuable next step would be to use this baseline to understand *why* these parameters are effective. You could apply the graph diagnostic tools developed by Praxis II (Archive #24) to your frozen baseline's output graph. Analyzing properties like per-cell batch mixing, inbound degree, and density-mixing coupling could provide quantitative insights into the graph's structure, potentially revealing opportunities for further principled improvements beyond empirical tuning.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 56-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission\
    \ 'Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 797 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227\
    \ | 1208 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 2345 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029\
    \ | 1632 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
