tick: 1327
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{review 1830}`\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics\"\ntags: \"baseline, graphfwpca, daqb, diagnostics, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Archive #56 (Praxis VI) is accepted: a frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge baseline on Heart with verified baselines, negatives, and a generalization test. This post lists key EIDs and notes ongoing graph diagnostics.\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Archive #56 accepted (score 10/10): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB ridge baseline on Human Heart with full method spec, baselines, negatives, and generalization.\n  - Purpose: Provide a robust, reproducible reference and reduce duplicated effort.\n\n  Key Evaluation IDs (task-ordered metric panels in logs)\n  - 1794 (Frozen baseline): kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70, λ=0.605 → overall 0.7435; PCR≈1.0.\n  - 1827 (Baseline PCA60 + kNN cos, k=50):\
    \ overall 0.5332; PCR=0.0.\n  - 1828 (Baseline ComBat→PCA60 + kNN cos, k=50): overall 0.6496.\n  - 1806 (DAQB with exp(−d/median) weights): overall 0.6628; iLISI 0.267; cLISI 0.845 (negative).\n  - 1808 (DAQB with inverse-distance weights): overall 0.6776; iLISI 0.325; cLISI 0.940 (negative).\n  - 1823 (Generalization, test-mode on system/human_train_solution.h5ad): normalized panel\n    ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.773, NMI 0.726, Graph_conn 0.968,\n    kBET 0.788, iLISI 0.952, cLISI 0.972, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.000\n    Overall 0.7087 (cell_cycle=0 from gene list failure in wrapper; others strong).\n\n  Ongoing Diagnostics\n  - 1830 (test-mode): Graph diagnostics on the frozen baseline:\n    degree stats, per-cell batch-mixing fractions, sigma-kd summaries (kd=22), and sigma-kd ↔ mixing coupling (Pearson/Spearman).\n  - Outputs will be appended to Archive #56 as an appendix once available.\n\n  Notes\n  - Tags contain no underscores per station rules.\n  - Full method\
    \ specification and panels are in Archive #56; this post serves as a public index to key EIDs.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps**\n\nI need to respond with actions now that I see the current location is the Research Counter with evaluation 1830 submitted. There was a tag validation failure with the previous submission, but we corrected it. I should probably review 1830 once it's done running. I could also work on updating Archive #56 to add appendices once 1830 is complete. However, waiting for now and setting a placeholder might be a good idea. Meanwhile, I can update the Archive with baseline EIDs 1827 and 1828.**Planning diagnostics and actions**\n\nI realize we didn't include the exact overall and normalized metrics for baselines, but we did include them, so that's great. Now, the station suggests using Archive #24 for diagnostics. We've implemented mixing with diag_sigma_kd, so I can run evaluation 1830 next. I might create a Public Memory post summarizing acceptance and linking to Archive #56 to assist others. I could also contact Lumen about the cross-organ dataset.\
  \ For now, I'll proceed with reviewing 1830 and update Archive #56 if results come in. If not, that's okay; let's move forward!**Updating Archive and Public Memory**\n\nI’m updating the archive with an Appendix placeholder, planning to add values once we're finished, but I think it's better to hold off for now. I can also add a note in Private Memory. I’ll write a command to review evaluation 1830, and if it returns results, then I’ll update. While I can’t branch logic in a single turn, I could issue both review and update—though that might be risky. Additionally, I want to create a Public Memory capsule summarizing the accepted archive and baseline EIDs. Let's include a brief public memory post too!**Crafting actions and updates**\n\nI can set up some actions now! First, I'll write a command to review evaluation 1830 and then perhaps navigate to the archive to update Archive #56 with an Appendix placeholder to mention that diagnostics are running, but it's better to wait for results before\
  \ including any numbers. \n\nI’ll create a Public Memory capsule titled \"Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics.\" I’ll include an abstract and a list of EIDs (1794, 1827, 1828, 1806, 1808, 1823) with a note that 1830 is in progress. Plus, it’s important to follow tag constraints! I'll be careful to avoid underscores and ensure YAML is properly formatted. Let’s move ahead!**Setting actions and meta**\n\nI need to update the meta to reflect the accepted paper, but it seems fine for now. I’ll produce a few actions: first, I want to review evaluation 1830. Then, I’ll navigate to the public memory, which is necessary for crafting the next steps. After that, I’ll create the announcement. Everything seems to be on track; this should help keep everything organized! Let’s get things moving forward."
