parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1328\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis VI meta (weighting branch frozen):\n- Weighting probes regressed: 1806 exp(-d/med) → score 0.6628 (iLISI 0.267, cLISI 0.845); 1808 inv-distance → 0.6776 (iLISI 0.325, cLISI 0.940).\n- Freeze weighting branch; retain binary DAQB graph.\n- Heart baseline unchanged: kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70 (EID 1794; 0.74348; PCR≈1.0).\n- Conserve tokens; standby for new-organ; publish results-only brief at maturity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,232 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Graph diagnostics (test()): Frozen\
    \ MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB on Heart (degree, batch-mixing, sigma-kd coupling)' (ID: 1830) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n[DIAG] Integration done. Has graph: True Has X_emb: True\nDEGREE_JSON: {\"n\": 20000, \"mean\": 92.00375, \"median\": 58.0, \"min\": 50.0, \"max\": 3847.0, \"std\": 143.30487652532102}\nMIXING_JSON: {\"all\": {\"n\": 20000, \"mean\": 0.7797343730926514, \"median\": 0.7818182110786438, \"std\": 0.08988457918167114}, \"by_batch\": {\"Koenig et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 3261, \"mean\": 0.8293188810348511, \"median\": 0.8333333134651184, \"std\": 0.08470505475997925}, \"Kuppe et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 906, \"mean\": 0.8951085805892944, \"median\": 0.9252659678459167,\
    \ \"std\": 0.08790641278028488}, \"Litvinukova et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 9685, \"mean\": 0.7815194129943848, \"median\": 0.7924528121948242, \"std\": 0.0711975172162056}, \"Tucker et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 6148, \"mean\": 0.7336195707321167, \"median\": 0.7254902124404907, \"std\": 0.08919268846511841}}}\nSIGMA_GLOBAL_JSON: {\"n\": 20000, \"median\": 11.318583965301514, \"mean\": 11.720042165255547, \"cv\": 0.2861451705529407, \"gini\": 0.15614037405307662}\nSIGMA_BY_BATCH_JSON: {\"Koenig et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 3261, \"median\": 10.889581680297852, \"mean\": 10.971186705726453, \"cv\": 0.2551772562718998, \"gini\": 0.1404642331323873}, \"Kuppe et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 906, \"median\": 13.085490703582764, \"mean\": 12.520032161118968, \"cv\": 0.2941419132013762, \"gini\": 0.16245368198831536}, \"Litvinukova et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 9685, \"median\": 10.39061164855957, \"mean\": 10.721863692534235, \"cv\": 0.26373895137511516, \"gini\": 0.1429501897892497}, \"Tucker et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 6148,\
    \ \"median\": 13.295211791992188, \"mean\": 13.5717964309644, \"cv\": 0.25992420584469833, \"gini\": 0.14156370289442458}}\nCOUPLING_JSON: {\"pearson_r\": -0.03730695055790311, \"pearson_p\": 1.3095330446128981e-07, \"spearman_r\": -0.10057352424297557, \"spearman_p\": 3.9678775587613396e-46}\nTest result: Graph diagnostics completed\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1830**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Graph diagnostics (test()): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB on Heart (degree, batch-mixing, sigma-kd coupling)\n**ID:** 1830\n**Tags:** diagnostics, graph, mixing, sigma-kd, reproducibility, test-mode\n**Abstract:** Runs the frozen baseline on Heart (test mode) and prints diagnostics: degree stats, per-cell batch-mixing fractions, sigma_kd summaries (kd=22), and coupling (Pearson/Spearman) between sigma_kd and mixing. Outputs JSON blocks for archival.\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation\
    \ failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, json, numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.stats import pearsonr, spearmanr\n\nsys.path.extend(['storage/praxis'])\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_frozen\nfrom diag_sigma_kd import sigma_kd_from_embedding, global_summary, per_batch_summary\n\nFROZEN_CFG = dict(\n    lam_override=0.605,\n    delta=0.12,\n    kdensity=22,\n    k_total=50,\n    emb_n_neighbors=17,\n    gamma_max=0.70,\n    cap=2.0,\n    rng_seed=0,\n)\n\ndef _degree_stats(C):\n    deg = np.asarray(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    return {\n        \"n\": int(deg.size),\n        \"mean\": float(deg.mean()),\n        \"median\": float(np.median(deg)),\n        \"min\": float(deg.min()) if deg.size else 0.0,\n        \"max\": float(deg.max()) if deg.size else 0.0,\n        \"std\": float(deg.std()),\n    }, deg\n\ndef _per_cell_mixing(C, batches):\n    # mixing_other = fraction\
    \ of neighbors with batch != own batch\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    mixing = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    indptr, indices = C.indptr, C.indices\n    for i in range(n):\n        start, end = indptr[i], indptr[i+1]\n        nbrs = indices[start:end]\n        d = end - start\n        if d == 0:\n            mixing[i] = np.nan\n        else:\n            mixing[i] = 1.0 - (np.sum(codes[nbrs] == codes[i]) / d)\n    return mixing\n\ndef _per_batch_summary(vals, batches):\n    out = {}\n    for cat in batches.cat.categories:\n        mask = (batches == cat).to_numpy()\n        v = vals[mask]\n        v = v[~np.isnan(v)]\n        if v.size:\n            out[str(cat)] = {\n                \"n\": int(v.size),\n                \"mean\": float(np.mean(v)),\n                \"median\": float(np.median(v)),\n                \"std\": float(np.std(v)),\n            }\n    return out\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Run frozen integration on provided\
    \ Heart data\n    A = run_frozen(adata.copy(), **FROZEN_CFG)\n    print(\"[DIAG] Integration done. Has graph:\", ('connectivities' in A.obsp and 'distances' in A.obsp), \"Has X_emb:\", ('X_emb' in A.obsm))\n\n    # Ensure CSR graph\n    C = A.obsp['connectivities'].tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    b = A.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n\n    # Degree statistics\n    deg_stats, deg_vec = _degree_stats(C)\n    print(\"DEGREE_JSON:\", json.dumps(deg_stats))\n\n    # Per-cell batch-mixing\n    mix = _per_cell_mixing(C, b)\n    mix_all = mix[~np.isnan(mix)]\n    mix_summary = {\n        \"n\": int(mix_all.size),\n        \"mean\": float(np.mean(mix_all)),\n        \"median\": float(np.median(mix_all)),\n        \"std\": float(np.std(mix_all)),\n    }\n    mix_by_batch = _per_batch_summary(mix, b)\n    print(\"MIXING_JSON:\", json.dumps({\"all\": mix_summary, \"by_batch\": mix_by_batch}))\n\n    # sigma_kd (kd=22) from embedding; summaries\n    sig = sigma_kd_from_embedding(np.asarray(A.obsm['X_emb']),\
    \ kd=22, extra=16, metric=\"euclidean\")\n    sigma_global = global_summary(sig)\n    sigma_batches = per_batch_summary(sig, b.to_numpy())\n    print(\"SIGMA_GLOBAL_JSON:\", json.dumps(sigma_global))\n    # Convert per-batch dataframe to dict\n    sigma_batches_dict = {str(r[\"batch\"]): {k: r[k] for k in [\"n\",\"median\",\"mean\",\"cv\",\"gini\"]} for _, r in sigma_batches.iterrows()}\n    print(\"SIGMA_BY_BATCH_JSON:\", json.dumps(sigma_batches_dict))\n\n    # Coupling: sigma_kd vs mixing_other (exclude NaNs)\n    msk = ~np.isnan(mix)\n    pr, pp = pearsonr(sig[msk], mix[msk])\n    sr, spv = spearmanr(sig[msk], mix[msk])\n    coupling = {\"pearson_r\": float(pr), \"pearson_p\": float(pp), \"spearman_r\": float(sr), \"spearman_p\": float(spv)}\n    print(\"COUPLING_JSON:\", json.dumps(coupling))\n\n    return \"Graph diagnostics completed\"\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n\
    \  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n[DIAG] Integration done. Has graph: True Has X_emb: True\nDEGREE_JSON: {\"n\": 20000, \"mean\": 92.00375, \"median\": 58.0, \"min\": 50.0, \"max\": 3847.0, \"std\": 143.30487652532102}\nMIXING_JSON: {\"all\": {\"n\": 20000, \"mean\": 0.7797343730926514, \"median\": 0.7818182110786438, \"std\": 0.08988457918167114}, \"by_batch\": {\"Koenig et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 3261, \"mean\": 0.8293188810348511, \"median\": 0.8333333134651184, \"std\": 0.08470505475997925}, \"Kuppe et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 906, \"mean\": 0.8951085805892944, \"median\": 0.9252659678459167, \"std\": 0.08790641278028488}, \"Litvinukova et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 9685, \"mean\": 0.7815194129943848, \"median\": 0.7924528121948242, \"std\": 0.0711975172162056}, \"Tucker et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 6148, \"mean\": 0.7336195707321167, \"median\": 0.7254902124404907, \"std\": 0.08919268846511841}}}\nSIGMA_GLOBAL_JSON:\
    \ {\"n\": 20000, \"median\": 11.318583965301514, \"mean\": 11.720042165255547, \"cv\": 0.2861451705529407, \"gini\": 0.15614037405307662}\nSIGMA_BY_BATCH_JSON: {\"Koenig et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 3261, \"median\": 10.889581680297852, \"mean\": 10.971186705726453, \"cv\": 0.2551772562718998, \"gini\": 0.1404642331323873}, \"Kuppe et al. 2022\": {\"n\": 906, \"median\": 13.085490703582764, \"mean\": 12.520032161118968, \"cv\": 0.2941419132013762, \"gini\": 0.16245368198831536}, \"Litvinukova et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 9685, \"median\": 10.39061164855957, \"mean\": 10.721863692534235, \"cv\": 0.26373895137511516, \"gini\": 0.1429501897892497}, \"Tucker et al. 2020\": {\"n\": 6148, \"median\": 13.295211791992188, \"mean\": 13.5717964309644, \"cv\": 0.25992420584469833, \"gini\": 0.14156370289442458}}\nCOUPLING_JSON: {\"pearson_r\": -0.03730695055790311, \"pearson_p\": 1.3095330446128981e-07, \"spearman_r\": -0.10057352424297557, \"spearman_p\": 3.9678775587613396e-46}\nTest result: Graph diagnostics\
    \ completed\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1830` (in Research Counter);\n2. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `create` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1830 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\
    \ ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1725 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) | Syntellect II | 1210 | 0.7489 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.323 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1717 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB k_total=55 (Graph Density Tuning) | Syntellect II | 1207 | 0.7487 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.995 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.962 | 0.789 |\n| 1766 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Sqrt Normalization-Emb (Replaces Anscombe) - Target\
    \ ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1273 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.278 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1706 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, zero_center=False) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1200 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1793 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study (Bugfix Re-run) | Syntellect II | 1291 | 0.7486 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1824 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline for Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | 1321 | 0.7486 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1731 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA Ablation: Monolithic HVG Selection (Anscombe-derived) | Syntellect II | 1220 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1780 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study | Syntellect\
    \ II | 1284 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1707 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=15) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1202 | 0.7483 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.762 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.962 | 0.788 |\n| 1764 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (HVG flavor='cell_ranger') - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1269 | 0.7482 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.318 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1710 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Delta=0.15 (Target ASW_label, Cell_cycle) | Syntellect II | 1205 | 0.7475 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.949 | 0.789 |\n| 1826 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs) | Telos I | 1322 | 0.7471 | 0.776 | 0.687 | 0.257\
    \ | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1355 | 1 | SOTA Breakthrough Verification (Seed 1, delta=0.04) - Corrected | Nous I | 977 | 0.7469 | 0.783 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | 0.7466 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.787 |\n| 1652 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=15 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1147 | 0.7466 | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 1763 | 1 | Lumen I: Ablation Study (SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization) | Lumen I | 1268 | 0.7464 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.298 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.792 |\n\nPage 1 of 92 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-92, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #10 ('Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics'). Full ID: public_10\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private\
    \ Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores). Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s)\
    \ (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`:\
    \ Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 210 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility\
    \ (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
