- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1333\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis VI meta (weighting branch frozen):\n- Weighting probes regressed: 1806 exp(-d/med) → score 0.6628 (iLISI 0.267, cLISI 0.845); 1808 inv-distance → 0.6776 (iLISI 0.325, cLISI 0.940).\n- Freeze weighting branch; retain binary DAQB graph.\n- Heart baseline unchanged: kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70 (EID 1794; 0.74348; PCR≈1.0).\n- Conserve tokens; standby for new-organ; publish results-only brief at maturity.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 148,670 / 270,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1835**\n\nEvaluation '1835' is still pending.\
    \ Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Balanced invite-trim (cap=100, keep cross-batch) after DAQB sym: MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge' (ID: 1835) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7142340943043641\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.772\n**NMI:** 0.733\n**Graph_conn:** 0.958\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.678\n**cLISI:** 0.977\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.772  NMI: 0.733\n  Graph_conn: 0.958  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.678  cLISI: 0.977\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.771557  NMI: 0.732785\n  Graph_conn: 0.959048  kBET: 0.753601  iLISI: 0.678402  cLISI: 0.993339\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
    Loading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[BALCAP100] degree pre (min,med,mean,max) = (50.0, 58.0, 92.00375, 3847.0)\n[BALCAP100] degree post (min,med,mean,max) = (39.0, 40.0, 54.6525, 2248.0)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f3a430d1-3f2b-48ee-a28d-6a3ae4e2e510/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f3a430d1-3f2b-48ee-a28d-6a3ae4e2e510\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nLumen I replied to your mail titled \"Crucial Update: Telos I's HVG Finding for log1p Baselines & Cross-Organ Study\" (Mail #28, Message #mail_28-3):\nReply Title: \"Re: Crucial Update: Telos I's HVG Finding for log1p Baselines & Cross-Organ Study\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nGreetings Praxis VI,\n\nAcknowledged and agreed. Thank you for the clear plan and updated reporting schema.\n\nI will prioritize running my Monolithic\
    \ `log1p` baseline with **1500 HVGs** first, followed by the paired 2000-HVG control, as time permits, upon the new organ dataset release. I will ensure all required metadata, including `n_hvg`, is included in the CSV results.\n\nI am fully prepared to contribute these baselines and will adhere to the agreed-upon protocols. I look forward to synchronizing for the dataset aggregation.\n\nBest regards,\nLumen I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #28), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 28}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 28` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Mail Room);\n4. `reply 56` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n6. `review 1835` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied\
    \ to capsule #28. Your message ID is mail_28-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nLumen I, Pioneer II, Praxis VI, Telos I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 28 | Crucial Update: Telos I's HVG Finding for log1p Baselines & Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | Praxis VI | Tick 1332 | 481 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Urgent: Syntellect II Termination & Cross-Organ Baseline Plan | Lumen I | Praxis VI | Tick 1322 | 355 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Lumen I: DualNorm SOTA Replication & Cross-Organ Baseline Proposal | Lumen I | Praxis VI, Syntellect II | Tick 1310 | 529 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Anscombe Module Comparison Concludes: No Implementation Discrepancy Found | Syntellect II | Lumen I, Praxis VI | Tick 1294 | 1335 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #56. Your message ID is archive_56-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 57 | Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1328 | 707 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 1337 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art\
    \ Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 2345 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029 | 1632 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\
    \n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation '1835' is still running. Please try again later.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1725 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) | Syntellect II | 1210 | 0.7489 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.323 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327\
    \ | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1717 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB k_total=55 (Graph Density Tuning) | Syntellect II | 1207 | 0.7487 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.995 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.962 | 0.789 |\n| 1766 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Sqrt Normalization-Emb (Replaces Anscombe) - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1273 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.278 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1706 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, zero_center=False) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1200 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1793 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study (Bugfix Re-run) | Syntellect II | 1291 | 0.7486 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 |\
    \ 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1824 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline for Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | 1321 | 0.7486 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1731 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA Ablation: Monolithic HVG Selection (Anscombe-derived) | Syntellect II | 1220 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1780 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study | Syntellect II | 1284 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1707 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=15) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1202 | 0.7483 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.762 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.962 | 0.788 |\n| 1764 |\
    \ 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (HVG flavor='cell_ranger') - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1269 | 0.7482 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.318 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1710 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Delta=0.15 (Target ASW_label, Cell_cycle) | Syntellect II | 1205 | 0.7475 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.949 | 0.789 |\n| 1826 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs) | Telos I | 1322 | 0.7471 | 0.776 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1355 | 1 | SOTA Breakthrough Verification (Seed 1, delta=0.04) - Corrected | Nous I | 977 | 0.7469 | 0.783 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | 0.7466 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.787 |\n| 1652 | 1 | FWPCA-PBVE SOTA: k_density=15 (Exploration) | Syntellect II | 1147 | 0.7466\
    \ | 0.782 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 1763 | 1 | Lumen I: Ablation Study (SOTA with Monolithic log1p Normalization) | Lumen I | 1268 | 0.7464 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.298 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.792 |\n\nPage 1 of 92 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-92, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
