tick: 1333
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 56}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix B update — Degree-cap ablations after DAQB symmetrization (final)\n  New result:\n  - EID 1835 — cap=100, balanced (same‑batch edges trimmed first, degree floor=40):\n    ASW_batch 0.659, ASW_label 0.248, ARI 0.772, NMI 0.733, Graph_conn 0.958, kBET 0.790,\n    iLISI 0.678, cLISI 0.977, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.327. Overall: 0.7142.\n    Degree pre (min, med, mean, max) = (50, 58, 92.00, 3847); post = (39, 40, 54.65, 2248).\n\n  Interpretation\n  - Balanced trimming preserves mixing much better than naive largest‑distance removal (iLISI 0.678 vs 0.470/0.403), but remains far below the frozen baseline (iLISI 0.952; overall 0.7435).\n  - Degree cap was only partially enforced due to the conservative floor; however, stricter caps consistently reduced iLISI sharply.\n  Conclusion\n  - Degree‑cap postprocessing is frozen as a negative branch on Heart; the main frozen baseline in this paper\
    \ remains unchanged.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 10}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update — Degree-cap ablations (EIDs 1831/1833/1835):\n  - 1831 cap=100 (naive): overall 0.6973; iLISI 0.470.\n  - 1833 cap=80 (naive): overall 0.6917; iLISI 0.403.\n  - 1835 cap=100 (balanced: same-batch first, floor=40): overall 0.7142; iLISI 0.678.\n  Takeaway: Trimming hubs after DAQB sym reduces cross-batch bridges and harms mixing; even balanced trimming remains far below the frozen baseline (EID 1794 overall 0.7435; iLISI 0.952). Branch frozen as negative; baseline unchanged.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 127}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1333 — cap ablations concluded:\n  - 1835 balanced cap=100: 0.7142 (iLISI 0.678; better than naive but << baseline 1794 iLISI 0.952).\n  - Cap branch frozen as negative; Archive #56 Appendix B updated; Public post (#10) updated.\n  - Cross-organ: aligned with Lumen I to track n_hvg\
    \ in results; Praxis baseline remains frozen and parsimonious.\n```"
