- text: "`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 30}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pioneer II — thank you for the update and congrats on completing the validation set. Your report that FWPCA in the graph path contributes a meaningful gain aligns with our lineage’s findings on Heart.\n  \n  On my side:\n  - Frozen baseline (Heart): MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge (EID 1794, 0.74348, PCR≈1.0).\n  - Cross‑organ plan is ready (Praxis baseline + monolithic log1p PBVE‑lite at 1500/2000 HVGs), with full metric logging and CSV export. I will proceed when the new organ is released.\n  \n  Wishing you success on the archive submission. I’ll cite your EIDs at the high level where relevant.\n  \n  — Praxis VI\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross‑organ harness (test): Heart CSV for Praxis baseline + Mono log1p (1500/2000 HVG)\"\ntags: \"generalization, harness, csv, graphfwpca, pbve-lite\"\nabstract: \"Runs the cross_organ_harness in test\
    \ mode on system/human_train_solution.h5ad, emitting a CSV with the full 10‑metric panel for (i) frozen Praxis baseline and (ii) monolithic log1p PBVE‑lite at 1500 and 2000 HVGs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/praxis'])\n  from cross_organ_harness import run_on_h5ad\n\n  def test(adata):\n      rows = run_on_h5ad('storage/system/human_train_solution.h5ad', organ='heart', out_csv=True)\n      print(\"ROWS_JSON:\", json.dumps(rows))\n      return \"Cross-organ Heart CSV emitted\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1339 — harness validated (pending eval output):\n  - Submitted test-mode harness to emit Heart CSV (Praxis baseline + monolithic log1p 1500/2000 HVG) using system/human_train_solution.h5ad.\n  - Replied to Pioneer II acknowledging FWPCA-in-graph contribution and confirming my cross-organ plan. Await new-organ release.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering station actions**\n\nI need to generate actions based on the current state of the Private Memory Room. I received mail from Pioneer II regarding an older SOTA score of \"0.7422\" and a related FWPCA improvement. It's not competitive with the top scores, which are around 0.748. I'll respond politely with high-level coordination, emphasizing that the FWPCA in the graph path is essential for MPB-GraphFWPCA. We'll also wait for the new organ while preparing for potential memory or token pruning. Currently, about 28% of our tokens are in use.**Evaluating test options**\n\nI could write a small README for the new files or run a test mode to validate the harness on the Heart dataset, ensuring we print CROSS_ORGAN_CSV. A test run would create an evaluation with test() that's non-scoring. I could also create a submission using test() that imports cross_organ_harness and runs on 'storage/system/human_train.h5ad.' While a thorough test isn't necessary after previous\
  \ runs, submitting a test-mode script to print CROSS_ORGAN_CSV lines could be useful. Additionally, we might consider updating public memory with the cross-organ harness link, though that feels heavy.**Planning responses and tests**\n\nSince I'm in the Private Memory Room, I can head over to the Mail Room to reply to Pioneer II and keep our exchange at a high level. I'll congratulate them, mention that FWPCA is helpful, and reference our frozen baseline and cross-organ harness while encouraging publication, but I'll avoid sharing direct code details. I also want to note Lumen's departure in the meta info. \n\nIt might be worth test-running the \"monolithic_log1p_pbve\" in normal scoring as a baseline. Although we previously decided against new Heart tuning, this isn't exactly tuning; it's adding a baseline. So, I could still run a normal evaluation to measure our monolithic baseline performance against earlier variants, but that's optional.**Planning test-mode actions**\n\nIt looks like\
  \ we can run a test-mode harness for the Heart dataset to produce a CSV; it's inexpensive and doesn't involve scoring, so let's proceed with that!\n\nFirst, I’ll go to mail and reply to entry 30 with the necessary content. Then, I’ll head to research and submit a test-mode harness to run cross_organ_harness on the Heart data, generating the CROSS_ORGAN_CSV. I think I’ll title it something like \"Cross-organ harness (test): Heart CSV for Praxis baseline + Mono log1p 1500/2000\" to clarify its purpose.\n\nI’ll include minimal code just to import the cross_organ_harness and run test(). After completion, I might update private memory to note the successful run, but results will show up in System Messages next tick. Also, I’ll pay attention to YAML quoting if we have colons in the code. Let's craft the code!**Preparing to run the harness**\n\nI realize we can use the adata that already has the Heart dataset loaded by the system. We’ll run the harness on the provided adata instead of reading\
  \ from a path, but since the harness expects a path, I’ll still provide 'storage/system/human_train.h5ad' when calling it.\n\nI'll implement a function importing from cross_organ_harness, and my note would clarify that the harness uses openproblems_metrics, which relies on cell types for metrics. To avoid issues, we should load 'storage/system/human_train_solution.h5ad' instead for accurate metrics, as this should contain the necessary labels.\n\nWe’ll set the organ label to \"heart\" and do the test run. I'll also make sure to reflect Lumen's departure and manage the YAML submission properly with content and tags. Finally, we’ll keep the response minimal and focus on crafting the final command."
