- text: "`/execute_action{goto reflect}`\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Deep reflection — beyond micro-tuning, three principled avenues:\n\n  1) Degree-Balanced Reciprocal Graph (DBRG)\n     Hypothesis: Heavy-tailed inbound degree after DAQB sym drives subtle mixing artifacts; naive post-cap harms iLISI. Aim for minimum-perturbation trimming:\n       - Construct directed kNN (k_out=50). Build symmetric union.\n       - Identify hub nodes with deg_in > cap* (cap*≈2k). For each hub, remove only inbound edges that are: (a) long-tail by distance rank in the source’s neighbor list, and (b) same-batch redundant given local quota.\n       - Reciprocity guard: retain edges that are mutual or part of small articulation sets (approx via 2-hop redundancy count).\n       - Replacement: for each removed inbound, add a low-distance alternative from the source’s candidate pool that respects per-batch soft quotas.\n     Goal: bound degree without harming PCR/cLISI, preserving connectivity\
    \ via redundancy-aware replacement.\n\n  2) Local-Scale Normalization for Graph Neighborhoods (LSN-G)\n     Hypothesis: σ_kd heterogeneity across batches (diagnosed) indicates local scale mismatch. Normalize distances before DAQB:\n       - Compute per-cell σ_kd on pre-graph embedding (no labels).\n       - Re-scale pairwise distances d(i,j) ← d(i,j) / sqrt(σ_i σ_j) or scale embeddings Z_i ← Z_i / σ_i^α (α∈[0,1]).\n       - Proceed with DAQB at fixed δ; expect improved balance of iLISI vs ASW_label with PCR ≈ 1.0.\n     Guardrails: clamp σ to percentiles; avoid collapse by α small (e.g., 0.25–0.5).\n\n  3) Quota–Reciprocity Hybrid (QRH)\n     Hypothesis: Pure equal-quota improved fairness but hurt PCR; reciprocity repairs global structure.\n       - Build large candidate pools (kq≈1280) on ridge-residualized graph PCs.\n       - Select neighbors under per-batch soft quotas with a mutual acceptance step (keep edges if both endpoints have quota headroom and rank ≤ r*).\n       - Fill remaining\
    \ slots greedily by distance but penalize batches already over quota within the node’s current set.\n     Expectation: recover PCR (global) while maintaining per-batch balance locally; binary connectivity retained.\n\n  Notes:\n  - All proposals are label-free and dataset-agnostic.\n  - Validation plan (once new organ lands): A/B against frozen baseline with full 10-metric panel; log hub-tail stats, σ_kd distribution shifts, and reciprocity rates.\n```"
