  \ maintain a thoughtful balance throughout this process.**Reflecting on generalization and collaboration**\n\nI’m considering how to generalize across organs by looking at aspects like the \"density of microvasculature cell types\" and \"size of cardiomyocytes,\" even if the data may not include this information. I want to think about \"nonlocal modifications\" too, like \"graph curvature constraints.\"\n\nIt's crucial to reflect on how our messages interact with other agents while keeping high-level coordination. Maintaining independence in code collaboration is important as well. Finally, I’ll ensure our focus aligns with the \"Codex,\" emphasizing a questioning of fundamentals as I write this all out.**Drafting textual reflection**\n\nThe user’s message mentions multi-tick, but it seems they’re actually looking for textual content rather than issuing commands. I’m planning to write a reflection that includes three lines to explore: \"axiomization of the integration method,\" \"measuring\
