role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage write praxis/cross_organ_harness.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, csv, io\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/system', 'storage/praxis'])\n  import openproblems_metrics as MET\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_praxis\n  from monolithic_log1p_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_mono_pbve\n\n  ORDER = [\"ASW_batch\",\"ASW_label\",\"ARI\",\"NMI\",\"Graph_conn\",\"kBET\",\"iLISI\",\"cLISI\",\"PCR\",\"Cell_cycle\"]\n  BASELINES_PATH = \"storage/system/openproblems_baselines.json\"\n\n  # Map task metric names -> possible baseline keys (lowercase) in JSON\n  BASE_KEY_MAP = {\n      \"ASW_batch\": [\"asw_batch\"],\n      \"ASW_label\": [\"asw_label\", \"isolated_label_asw\"],  # prefer asw_label; fallback allowed\n      \"ARI\": [\"ari\"],\n      \"NMI\": [\"nmi\"],\n      \"Graph_conn\": [\"graph_connectivity\"],\n      \"kBET\": [\"kbet\"],\n      \"iLISI\"\
    : [\"ilisi\"],\n      \"cLISI\": [\"clisi\"],\n      \"PCR\": [\"pcr\"],\n      \"Cell_cycle\": [\"cell_cycle_conservation\"],\n  }\n\n  PRAXIS_CFG = dict(\n      lam_override=0.605, delta=0.12, kdensity=22, k_total=50,\n      emb_n_neighbors=17, gamma_max=0.70, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n  )\n\n  def _safe_float(x):\n      try:\n          return float(x)\n      except Exception:\n          return float('nan')\n\n  def _load_baselines():\n      try:\n          with open(BASELINES_PATH, \"r\") as f:\n              data = json.load(f)\n          # Flatten if wrapped\n          if isinstance(data, dict) and \"baselines\" in data:\n              data = data[\"baselines\"]\n          # Normalize keys to lowercase for matching\n          lower = {str(k).lower(): v for k, v in data.items()}\n          table = {}\n          for k in ORDER:\n              lo, hi = 0.0, 1.0\n              for cand in BASE_KEY_MAP.get(k, []):\n                  if cand in lower:\n                      v = lower[cand]\n\
    \                      lo = _safe_float(v.get(\"min\", lo))\n                      hi = _safe_float(v.get(\"max\", hi))\n                      break\n              table[k] = {\"min\": lo, \"max\": hi}\n          return table\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"BASELINES_WARNING:\", repr(e))\n          return {k: {\"min\": 0.0, \"max\": 1.0} for k in ORDER}\n\n  def _normalize(raw: dict, baselines: dict):\n      norm = {}\n      for k in ORDER:\n          v = _safe_float(raw.get(k, np.nan))\n          lo = baselines[k][\"min\"]; hi = baselines[k][\"max\"]\n          if np.isnan(v) or hi == lo:\n              norm[k] = float('nan')\n          else:\n              z = (v - lo) / (hi - lo)\n              norm[k] = float(max(0.0, min(1.0, z)))\n      return norm\n\n  def _final_score(norm: dict):\n      vals = [norm.get(k, np.nan) for k in ORDER]\n      arr = np.array([x for x in vals if not np.isnan(x)], dtype=float)\n      return float(arr.mean()) if arr.size > 0 else float('nan')\n\
    \n  def _compute_raw_metrics(adata_integrated: ad.AnnData, adata_original: ad.AnnData):\n      # Process integration to expected format\n      P = MET.process_integration_output(adata_integrated, adata_original)\n      # Metrics\n      asw_batch = MET.compute_asw_batch(P)\n      asw_label = MET.compute_asw_label(P)\n      co = MET.compute_clustering_overlap(P)  # {'ari','nmi',...}\n      graph_conn = MET.compute_graph_connectivity(P)\n      kbet = MET.compute_kbet(P)\n      lisi = MET.compute_lisi(P)  # {'ilisi','clisi'}\n      pcr = MET.compute_pcr(adata_original, P)\n      cell_cycle = MET.compute_cell_cycle_conservation(adata_original, P)\n      raw = {\n          \"ASW_batch\": _safe_float(asw_batch),\n          \"ASW_label\": _safe_float(asw_label),\n          \"ARI\": _safe_float(co.get(\"ari\", np.nan)),\n          \"NMI\": _safe_float(co.get(\"nmi\", np.nan)),\n          \"Graph_conn\": _safe_float(graph_conn),\n          \"kBET\": _safe_float(kbet),\n          \"iLISI\": _safe_float(lisi.get(\"\
    ilisi\", np.nan)),\n          \"cLISI\": _safe_float(lisi.get(\"clisi\", np.nan)),\n          \"PCR\": _safe_float(pcr),\n          \"Cell_cycle\": _safe_float(cell_cycle),\n      }\n      return raw\n\n  def _count_hvg(A: ad.AnnData) -> int:\n      try:\n          if \"batch_hvg\" in A.var.columns:\n              return int(np.asarray(A.var[\"batch_hvg\"].values).astype(bool).sum())\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return int(A.n_vars)\n\n  def eval_method(adata_original: ad.AnnData, integrate_fn, cfg: dict | None):\n      B = integrate_fn(adata_original.copy(), **cfg) if cfg else integrate_fn(adata_original.copy())\n      raw = _compute_raw_metrics(B, adata_original)\n      bl = _load_baselines()\n      norm = _normalize(raw, bl)\n      score = _final_score(norm)\n      return raw, norm, score\n\n  def run_on_h5ad(path: str, organ: str, out_csv: bool = True):\n      A = ad.read_h5ad(path)  # solution dataset with labels\n      rows = []\n\n      # Praxis frozen\n   \
    \   raw, norm, score = eval_method(A, run_praxis, PRAXIS_CFG)\n      row = {\n          \"organ\": organ, \"method\": \"Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB\",\n          \"n_hvg\": _count_hvg(A), \"kd\": 22, \"k\": 50, \"delta\": 0.12,\n          \"emb_k\": 17, \"gamma_max\": 0.70, \"lambda\": 0.605, \"degree_cap\": \"none\",\n          \"overall\": _safe_float(score),\n      }\n      for k in ORDER:\n          row[k] = _safe_float(norm.get(k, np.nan))\n      rows.append(row)\n\n      # Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (1500 and 2000 HVGs)\n      for n_hvg in (1500, 2000):\n          raw, norm, score = eval_method(A, run_mono_pbve, {\"n_hvg\": int(n_hvg), \"n_pcs\": 60})\n          row = {\n              \"organ\": organ, \"method\": f\"Monolithic_log1p_PBVE_lite_n{n_hvg}\",\n              \"n_hvg\": int(n_hvg), \"kd\": \"n/a\", \"k\": 50, \"delta\": \"n/a\",\n              \"emb_k\": \"n/a\", \"gamma_max\": \"n/a\", \"lambda\": \"n/a\", \"degree_cap\": \"none\",\n              \"overall\": _safe_float(score),\n\
    \          }\n          for k in ORDER:\n              row[k] = _safe_float(norm.get(k, np.nan))\n          rows.append(row)\n\n      if out_csv:\n          buf = io.StringIO()\n          fieldnames = [\"organ\",\"method\",\"n_hvg\",\"kd\",\"k\",\"delta\",\"emb_k\",\"gamma_max\",\"lambda\",\"degree_cap\",\"overall\"] + list(ORDER)\n          w = csv.DictWriter(buf, fieldnames=fieldnames)\n          w.writeheader()\n          for r in rows: w.writerow(r)\n          print(\"CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\\n\" + buf.getvalue())\n      return rows\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Cross‑organ harness (test, v4): Correct baseline key mapping + CSV\"\ntags: \"generalization, harness, csv, metrics, openproblems\"\nabstract: \"Adds explicit mapping from task metric names (ASW_batch, Graph_conn, PCR, Cell_cycle, etc.) to the lowercase keys in system/openproblems_baselines.json, then runs the in‑station metric pipeline and emits a CSV for Praxis baseline and monolithic log1p (1500/2000\
    \ HVGs) on human_train_solution.h5ad.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/praxis'])\n  from cross_organ_harness import run_on_h5ad\n\n  def test(adata):\n      rows = run_on_h5ad('storage/system/human_train_solution.h5ad', organ='heart', out_csv=True)\n      print(\"ROWS_JSON:\", json.dumps(rows))\n      return \"Cross-organ Heart CSV emitted (v4)\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{review 1844}`"
thinking_content: "**Exploring normalization expectations**\n\nI'm looking into normalization, which requires minimum and maximum values for certain keys, typically between 0 to 1. This applies to metrics like Graph_conn and PCR, as well as ARI and NMI. We're actually cloning across proper ranges, but our normalized differences won't match the official pipeline since that relies on a different baseline. It seems I shouldn't worry too much about the test mode showing 'Evaluation failed' since it’s expected behavior. Alright, let’s focus on producing the full CSV results for v3!**Planning evaluation actions**\n\nI’m considering what actions to take next. I could show storage reads of outputs or review evaluation logs with a command. However, the research room for reviewing logs is only accessible for finished evaluations, and the message about the evaluation hasn’t completed yet. So, I'll need to wait for the next tick to check for the evaluation's status. Meanwhile, I can fix normalization\
  \ by mapping lowercase keys to uppercase names using synonyms, which sounds like a solid plan!**Reviewing baseline details**\n\nI need to check the content of 'openproblems_baselines.json' to confirm entries. I see that it includes 'isolated_label_asw' and 'isolated_label_f1', while I use 'ASW_label' for silhouettes. Good, I’ll align that with the baseline. For Graph_conn, I’ll use 'graph_connectivity', and for others like 'cell_cycle_conservation', 'pcr', and 'kbet', those seem good too. I should ensure that clustering overlap returns its keys in lower-case ('ari', 'nmi') mapped to uppercase. I also need to make sure that writing 'CROSS_ORGAN_CSV' works properly. Lastly, I’ll hold off until I get the results for evaluation 1844 and consider updating my meta or private memory.**Implementing code modifications**\n\nI'm ready to execute some actions! First, I'll use a command to patch the mapping and submit new test v4 to get numbers with normalized baselines. For the code changes, I’ll\
  \ start with _load_baselines to read the JSON and create a mapping from uppercase to a list of lowercase synonyms. I should also incorporate an optional calculation for normalization from the baseline. \n\nNext, I’ll ensure that YAML content is properly quoted. Finally, I might review evaluation 1844 to check its status, even though I know it might fail if it's not finished. I think I'm set to implement these!"
