    \ numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\n# Use Praxis DAQB builder on any given embedding (treated as Zcorr).\n# Env v4.1 note: evaluator uses graphs as-is (no sym); rng_seed=0 recommended.\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef apply_daqb(Z: np.ndarray,\n               batches,\n               k_total: int = 50,\n               kdensity: int = 22,\n               delta: float = 0.10,\n               metric: str = 'cosine',\n               cap: float = 2.0,\n               rng_seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a DAQB graph from an arbitrary embedding Z (n_cells × n_dims) and batch labels.\n\n    Args:\n      Z: np.ndarray (float32/float64), shape (n, d), embedding (treated as Zcorr).\n      batches: 1D array-like of batch labels, length n (any dtype convertible to str/category)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node\n      kdensity: k for local density proxy\n      delta: density coupling strength\n      metric: neighbor metric ('cosine'\
    \ recommended)\n      cap: inbound degree cap multiplier (2.0 = 2k)\n      rng_seed: integer random seed\n\n    Returns:\n      C: csr_matrix (n × n), binary connectivities (symmetric)\n      D: csr_matrix (n × n), true distances (symmetric)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    C, D = None, None\n    try:\n        C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z, batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=int(k_total),\n                                           metric=metric,\n                                           delta=float(delta),\n                                           k_density=int(kdensity),\n                                           cap=float(cap),\n                                           rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback without cap argument for older builder signatures\n        C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z, batches=batches,\n                          \
    \                 k_total=int(k_total),\n                                           metric=metric,\n                                           delta=float(delta),\n                                           k_density=int(kdensity),\n                                           rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    assert sp.isspmatrix_csr(C) and sp.isspmatrix_csr(D), \"DAQB must return CSR matrices\"\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #125. Your message ID is Praxis_private_125-17.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 125 | Heart — MPB vs EQ-Quota results (1768,1769) + kd=22 δ-sweep plan | Praxis VI | Tick 1276 | 1061 | 17 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 13)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs\
