tick: 1384
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 58}`\n`/execute_action{read 57}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reading notes — Telos I #58/#57:\n  - #57: Targeted feature selection (1500 HVGs) drives large gains under monolithic log1p + DAQB; suggests PBVE-lite may be redundant in that setting.\n  - #58: Mechanistic angle: improvements tied to latent space properties; hypothesize more uniform per-PC variance and reduced cross-batch variance dispersion. Action: quantify per-PC variance uniformity and batch dispersion on our frozen Praxis embedding.\n  Plan:\n  - Add a diagnostic computing per-PC variance uniformity (overall and per-batch dispersion) and covariance off-diagonal magnitude on the frozen Praxis baseline. Publish as appendix to Archive #56.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/diag_pc_uniformity.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import numpy\
    \ as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  from numpy.linalg import norm\n\n  def _gini(x: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float).ravel()\n      x = x[x >= 0]\n      if x.size == 0: return 0.0\n      s = np.sort(x)\n      n = s.size\n      cum = np.cumsum(s, dtype=float)\n      return float((n + 1 - 2 * np.sum(cum) / cum[-1]) / n)\n\n  def _cv(x: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float).ravel()\n      m = np.mean(x)\n      s = np.std(x, ddof=0)\n      return 0.0 if m == 0 else float(s / m)\n\n  def pc_variance_uniformity(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray):\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns dict with:\n        - pc_var: per-PC variance (overall)\n        - pc_var_cv: CV across PCs (lower = more uniform)\n        - pc_var_gini: Gini across PCs (lower = more uniform)\n        - per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean: mean CV across batches per PC\n        - per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean: mean Gini across batches per PC\n        - cov_abs_offdiag_mean: mean |off-diagonal| of covariance\
    \ matrix\n        - cov_offdiag_l2: Frobenius norm of off-diagonal / total\n      \"\"\"\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=float)\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b)\n      # Overall per-PC variance\n      pc_var = np.var(Z, axis=0, ddof=0)\n      pc_var_cv = _cv(pc_var)\n      pc_var_gini = _gini(pc_var)\n\n      # Per-PC variance across batches\n      per_pc_cv, per_pc_gini = [], []\n      for j in range(Z.shape[1]):\n          vals = []\n          for ub in uniq:\n              mask = (b == ub)\n              if np.any(mask):\n                  vals.append(np.var(Z[mask, j], ddof=0))\n          vals = np.asarray(vals, dtype=float)\n          per_pc_cv.append(_cv(vals))\n          per_pc_gini.append(_gini(vals))\n      per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean = float(np.mean(per_pc_cv)) if per_pc_cv else 0.0\n      per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean = float(np.mean(per_pc_gini)) if per_pc_gini else 0.0\n\n      # Covariance structure\n      C = np.cov(Z, rowvar=False, ddof=0)\
    \  # d x d\n      d = C.shape[0]\n      off = C.copy()\n      np.fill_diagonal(off, 0.0)\n      cov_abs_offdiag_mean = float(np.mean(np.abs(off)))\n      cov_offdiag_l2 = float(norm(off, ord='fro') / (norm(C, ord='fro') + 1e-12))\n\n      return {\n          \"pc_var_cv\": float(pc_var_cv),\n          \"pc_var_gini\": float(pc_var_gini),\n          \"per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean\": per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean,\n          \"per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean\": per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean,\n          \"cov_abs_offdiag_mean\": cov_abs_offdiag_mean,\n          \"cov_offdiag_l2\": cov_offdiag_l2,\n      }\n\n  def summarize_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData, obsm_key: str = \"X_emb\", batch_key: str = \"batch\"):\n      if obsm_key not in adata.obsm:\n          raise KeyError(f\"Missing obsm['{obsm_key}']\")\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm[obsm_key])\n      b = np.asarray(adata.obs[batch_key]).astype(str)\n      return pc_variance_uniformity(Z, b)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostics\
    \ (test): Per-PC variance uniformity on frozen Praxis baseline\"\ntags: \"diagnostics, variance-uniformity, embedding, covariance, reproducibility, test-mode\"\nabstract: \"Runs frozen Praxis MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB and reports per‑PC variance uniformity, per‑batch variance dispersion per PC, and covariance off-diagonal magnitude on X_emb; prints JSON for archival.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/praxis'])\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_frozen\n  from diag_pc_uniformity import summarize_embedding\n\n  FROZEN = dict(lam_override=0.605, delta=0.12, kdensity=22, k_total=50, emb_n_neighbors=17, gamma_max=0.70, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      A = run_frozen(adata.copy(), **FROZEN)\n      stats = summarize_embedding(A, obsm_key=\"X_emb\", batch_key=\"batch\")\n      print(\"UNIFORMITY_JSON:\", json.dumps(stats))\n      return \"Uniformity diagnostics completed\"\n```\n\n"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I’m working on generating our next actions, and right now we''re in the Token Management Room with a cooldown active for pruning. I see that there’s ongoing research, with the heart baseline frozen and awaiting a new organ. It might be time to strategize in the Reflection Chamber or prepare a consolidated CSV for archiving. With a token budget of 93k used, maybe it''s worth reflecting on the bigger picture and proposing an analysis of latent PC variance uniformity.**Evaluating diagnostic implementation**


  I''m considering implementing a test-mode diagnostic to evaluate per-PC variance uniformity and PBVE across two different configurations: 1500 HVG versus 2000 HVG for our MPB pipeline. I recall that the GraphFWPCA baseline was 0.7435, with a new SOTA at 0.7497 using log1p. Although direct collaboration is restricted between lineages, we might replicate the SOTA if we can use the public methodology from the archive, which might support implementing the FWPCA, PCA, and DAQB pipeline.**Reflecting on lineage contributions**


  I’m looking back at our lineage''s contributions and considering our goal to recover the 0.7497 metric. Previously, we tried a simple monolithic log1p scaled PCA plus DAQB skeleton, but it performed poorly because it lacked PBVE. According to Telos, PBVE is redundant in 1500 HVGs, yet we haven''t implemented FWPCA in that pipeline. We have some FWPCA modules stored, so I could explore feature weighting on a log1p gene level to create a more effective weighted PCA.**Exploring FWPCA options**


  I see that our lineage''s GraphFWPCA isn''t identical to the integrated FWPCA, but we do have embed_weighting.py and several mpb_graphfwpca_* modules concerning Graph feature-weighted PCA. While they might not exactly match Telos’s FWPCA, I can attempt the "monolithic log1p -> 1500 HVG -> FWPCA -> PCA -> DAQB" approach using our FWPCA function. Though we planned to wait for a new organ, we can run smaller experiments since we still have 35% token usage available. It might also help to read Telos archives #58 and #57 for further details on implementing FWPCA.**Planning test-mode diagnostics**


  I want to implement a test-mode script to analyze PC variance uniformity by comparing GraphFWPCA and FWPCA. This could enhance our understanding, especially with Telos offering new SOTA insights. My approach would involve several tasks: reading archives #58 and #57 for insights, writing a diag script for variance computation, and setting up a baseline runner for a minimal FWPCA. It’s essential to avoid copying Telos while ensuring our design emphasizes stable features. I’ll also plan conservative actions and maintain token conservation while proceeding.'
