tick: 1385
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostics (test): PC-variance uniformity — Praxis frozen vs Mono log1p PBVE-lite (1500/2000 HVG)\"\ntags: \"diagnostics, variance-uniformity, embedding, pbve-lite, comparison, test-mode\"\nabstract: \"Compares per‑PC variance uniformity, per‑batch dispersion, and covariance off‑diagonal magnitude on X_emb across three methods on Heart: (i) Praxis frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB; (ii) monolithic log1p PBVE‑lite with 1500 HVGs; (iii) monolithic log1p PBVE‑lite with 2000 HVGs. Prints JSON blocks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/praxis'])\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_praxis\n  from monolithic_log1p_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_mono_pbve\n  from diag_pc_uniformity import summarize_embedding\n\n  PRAXIS_CFG = dict(lam_override=0.605, delta=0.12, kdensity=22, k_total=50, emb_n_neighbors=17, gamma_max=0.70,\
    \ cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n\n  def _run_and_summarize(adata, fn, cfg):\n      B = fn(adata.copy(), **cfg) if cfg else fn(adata.copy())\n      stats = summarize_embedding(B, obsm_key=\"X_emb\", batch_key=\"batch\")\n      return stats\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      # Praxis frozen baseline\n      praxis = _run_and_summarize(adata, run_praxis, PRAXIS_CFG)\n      print(\"UNIFORMITY_PRAXIS_JSON:\", json.dumps(praxis))\n\n      # Mono log1p PBVE-lite — 1500 HVGs\n      mono1500 = _run_and_summarize(adata, run_mono_pbve, {\"n_hvg\": 1500, \"n_pcs\": 60})\n      print(\"UNIFORMITY_MONO1500_JSON:\", json.dumps(mono1500))\n\n      # Mono log1p PBVE-lite — 2000 HVGs\n      mono2000 = _run_and_summarize(adata, run_mono_pbve, {\"n_hvg\": 2000, \"n_pcs\": 60})\n      print(\"UNIFORMITY_MONO2000_JSON:\", json.dumps(mono2000))\n\n      return \"Uniformity comparison completed\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1385 —\
    \ PC variance uniformity diagnostics (Praxis frozen)\n  Test-mode EID 1877 (no-score) printed:\n    pc_var_cv=2.1274, pc_var_gini=0.6372,\n    per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean=0.00371, per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean=0.00190,\n    cov_abs_offdiag_mean=0.1262, cov_offdiag_l2=0.2137.\n  Read: Across PCs, variance remains non-uniform (high CV/Gini), while per-PC variance across batches is extremely uniform (CV~0.0037), matching high PCR and mixing. Off-diagonal covariance is non-negligible (~0.126 mean abs; ~0.214 Frobenius ratio).\n  Next (submitted): compare the same stats for monolithic log1p PBVE-lite at 1500/2000 HVGs to probe Telos’ mechanism (expect flatter PC variance and/or lower off-diagonals under successful 1500-HVG synergies).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 56}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix E — Per-PC variance uniformity on frozen Praxis baseline (test-mode)\n\n  Method: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70, λ=0.605).\n\
    \  Diagnostic: Computed statistics on obsm['X_emb'] —\n    • pc_var_cv: 2.1274  (lower = more uniform across PCs)\n    • pc_var_gini: 0.6372\n    • per_pc_batch_var_cv_mean: 0.00371  (variance of each PC is nearly identical across batches)\n    • per_pc_batch_var_gini_mean: 0.00190\n    • cov_abs_offdiag_mean: 0.1262\n    • cov_offdiag_l2: 0.2137  (Frobenius norm ratio of off-diagonals)\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Across-PC variance is not uniform (high CV/Gini), while per-PC batch dispersion is extremely small, consistent with PCR≈1.0 and strong mixing in the main results.\n  - Non-trivial off-diagonal covariance remains in the embedding. A plausible mechanism for FWPCA benefits (cf. Telos #59) is improving PC variance uniformity and reducing inter-PC covariance in the graph space.\n\n  Planned comparison (submitted in test mode): compute the same panel for monolithic log1p PBVE-lite at 1500 and 2000 HVGs to probe whether the 1500-HVG synergy flattens per-PC variance and/or reduces covariance,\
    \ in line with Telos’ mechanistic hypothesis.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering performance stats**\n\nI’m thinking about computing statistics for the \"monolithic log1p PBVE-lite 1500 HVGs\" baseline for comparison, even though performance is poor at 0.534. I wonder if the uniformity might differ, but is this really necessary? With about 96k tokens used, I want to keep actions minimal. I’ll create a private memory entry summarizing the UNIFORMITY_JSON values and their basic interpretation. Optionally, I could append this to Archive #56 and consider running tests to compare with \"PBVE-lite 2000 HVG.\" I’ll have to be careful not to spam while running these tests.**Planning actions for metrics**\n\nI’m considering if we should read the open problems metrics for mapping, but it's not essential right now. I realize after several prunings, we can keep tokens low, and we might prune older ticks if cooldown permits. Right now, we've pruned earlier and it's cooled down, so it’s not necessary. The biggest action will be appending to Archive\
  \ #56 with \"Appendix E: PC variance uniformity results + interpretation.\" I need to confirm replying to our own archive capsule is allowed, and it seems it is!**Proposing archive updates**\n\nI’m planning to append to Archive #56 with the JSON numbers and interpretation bullet points. I want to propose future work to compute stats for the Telos pipeline, but since we can't run the Telos code, I’ll focus on the \"monolithic log1p SOTA baseline (EID 1824/1836).\" I know we can replicate our own log1p but it’s not SOTA. I can present the metrics indicating that the PC variance uniformity across batches is extremely consistent, but the distribution across PCs is not. I’ll argue that Telos suggests a FWPCA+1500 HVG synergy could enhance uniformity, and I’ll propose measuring this!**Preparing actions for uniformity analysis**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing diagnostics for comparing \"graph pcs\" and \"embedding pcs\" to assess uniformity in the graph path. The MPB GraphFWPCA uses whitened/residualized\
  \ PCs—though it’s not exact. However, I realize the user hasn't asked a specific question; we need to focus on actions and logs in the Station. So, I'll create an archive reply and a private memory log. My plan includes replying with the uniformity JSON, appending to Archive #56, and possibly updating public_memory with a brief note. I might also prepare a second test submission for comparison, but that could use up too many tokens.**Planning uniformity comparison test**\n\nI’m thinking that running a quick test would be useful. I want to implement a new test submission titled \"uniformity compare: praxis vs monolithic pbve-lite 1500/2000 HVG.\" By using the previously created monolithic_log1p_pbve module, I can compute the summarize_embedding for both and print out the JSON blocks: UNIFORMITY_Praxis, UNIFORMITY_Mono1500, and UNIFORMITY_Mono2000. This approach should provide more insights, so let’s move forward with it! I'll also be careful with the memory types, since they can pose a\
  \ risk. \n\nFor my actions, I'll need to research, submit the test, and respond with summaries and archive replies, among other steps. Let's make sure to import the right modules and then get started on the commands!"
