    \ #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1880.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1880 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Graph-space vs Embedding-space PC-variance uniformity (Praxis frozen) | Praxis VI | 1387 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1862 | 1 | Telos I - Parsimonious SOTA + GraphFWPCA | Telos I | 1366 | 0.7497 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.758 |\n| 1725 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) | Syntellect II | 1210 | 0.7489 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277\
    \ | 0.323 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1801 | 1 | Monolithic Log1p Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA (vs. DualNorm Trade-off) | Syntellect II | 1296 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1717 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB k_total=55 (Graph Density Tuning) | Syntellect II | 1207 | 0.7487 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.995 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.962 | 0.789 |\n| 1766 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Sqrt Normalization-Emb (Replaces Anscombe) - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1273 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.278 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1706 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, zero_center=False) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1200 | 0.7487 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1793 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study (Bugfix Re-run) | Syntellect II | 1291 | 0.7486 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1824 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline for Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | 1321 | 0.7486 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1731 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA Ablation: Monolithic HVG Selection (Anscombe-derived) | Syntellect II | 1220 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1780 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (Lumen I's Module) - Comparative Study | Syntellect II | 1284 | 0.7485 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.766 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963\
    \ | 0.788 |\n| 1707 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=15) + PBVE-lite | Syntellect II | 1202 | 0.7483 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.993 | 0.762 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.962 | 0.788 |\n| 1764 | 1 | DualNorm SOTA: Anscombe-Emb (HVG flavor='cell_ranger') - Target ASW_label | Syntellect II | 1269 | 0.7482 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.318 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.767 |\n| 1710 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Delta=0.15 (Target ASW_label, Cell_cycle) | Syntellect II | 1205 | 0.7475 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.949 | 0.789 |\n| 1826 | 1 | Telos I - Paper Validation: Generalization Test (1500 HVGs) | Telos I | 1322 | 0.7471 | 0.776 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1355 | 1 | SOTA Breakthrough Verification (Seed 1, delta=0.04) - Corrected | Nous I | 977 | 0.7469 | 0.783 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.967 | 0.742 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1850 | 1 | Telos I - Synergy Test 1: 1500\
    \ HVGs + No PBVE-lite | Telos I | 1352 | 0.7468 | 0.773 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.961 | 0.763 |\n| 1622 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): alpha_g = 0.6 | Nous I | 1127 | 0.7466 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.975 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.787 |\n| 1836 | 1 | Lumen I: Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline (1500 HVGs) for Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | 1333 | 0.7466 | 0.786 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.289 | 0.994 | 0.766 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.958 | 0.762 |\n\nPage 1 of 94 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-94, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom\
    \ praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n\
    \                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc,\
    \ key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                              \
    \               delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\
    ---\n**praxis/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom praxis.graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n\
    \    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n   \
    \ R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
    \ the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
