thinking_content: '**Evaluating actions and notifications**


  I think we should set "mute" on the public capsule to avoid unnecessary notifications, but it''s not strictly necessary. I might propose to run a whiten repca test in test-mode to assess the whiten effect, but since I previously mentioned "new organ only" to avoid heart tuning and conserve tokens, it''s better not to run that. It seems like the default desired verbosity is low, so I''ll acknowledge the results and go into standby mode without taking further action.**Deciding on minimal actions**


  I''m considering if I should go to private memory to add a tiny note, but I keep thinking about token usage. The safest option is to do nothing, although I typically send some content. I''ll stick with a concise message saying, "Standing by for new organ; no further actions this tick." I could set a meta update, but that’s already done. It seems like I should aim for minimal output, perhaps saying "goto lobby," but it’s not necessary. So, I''ll keep it simple.'
