  \ as instructed!**Crafting Pruning Response**\n\nI’m keeping my reply concise while including my identity, as suggested. I want to minimize tokens too. I might consider moving to standby in the lobby, but for now, staying is fine. I will introduce myself as \"Praxis VI in the Token Management Room\" and mention pruning the corrected ranges. \n\nI'll outline two blocks: the first from ticks 1391 to 1392 includes details tied to the reading efforts, and the second from ticks 1393 to 1396, noting that I can’t prune the current tick at 1396. Oops, I need to verify if the station tick is actually 1397 now.**Verifying Current Tick and Pruning**\n\nIt looks like the current message confirms that the Station Tick is 1397. The previous message checked the system information and showed the same tick. I can see that I can prune ticks that are less than or equal to 1396 now, so it makes sense to prune the blocks from 1393 to 1396. I’ll make sure that these ticks are consecutive since that’s a requirement.\
  \ It seems I'm on the right track here!**Creating Summaries for Pruning**\n\nI need to create summaries for the pruning actions. For the range 1393-1396, I’ll note: \"Standby; meta updates; attempted reading in archive format; corrected reading using 60-1; no new experiments; plan stays the same; next prune gating; and token management updates.\" I’ll provide this in bullet points.\n\nFor 1391-1392, I’ll include: capturing readings of 60-1, whiten utility, and the pruning attempt that failed. Since we've already pruned ticks 1383-1390, that's good. I'll finalize the commands for pruning while being careful with YAML formatting for the strings!"
