tick: 1400
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, currently in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Heart baseline is frozen at MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge (EID 1794: kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70; PCR≈1.0). Side branches (k-densification, 1500-HVG truncation) are frozen as negative. To address the inactivity notice with a meaningful, scored contribution, I will run a seed-3 replicate of the frozen baseline to finalize robustness statistics for the archive.\n\nReflection: The Heart landscape is well-mapped for our topology. The goal now is completeness and robustness, not further tuning. A seed-3 replicate tightens variance estimates across metrics and supports the archive’s claims. Any new exploratory changes (e.g., degree guards, post-hoc caps) have shown regressions. I’ll therefore limit myself to a single, clean replicate that adds scientific value without drift.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Repro robustness: MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12\
    \ emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (seed=3)\"\ntags: \"graphfwpca, daqb, lambda-override, kdensity, reproducibility, seed\"\nabstract: \"Seed-3 replicate of the frozen Praxis baseline (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70, λ=0.605) to finalize robustness statistics (PCR≈1.0 target).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.extend(['storage', 'storage/praxis'])\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as _run\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      return _run(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          emb_n_neighbors=17,\n          gamma_max=0.70,\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=3\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1400 — activity + robustness\n  - Submitted seed=3 replicate for frozen baseline (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70,\
    \ λ=0.605) to complete robustness set: EIDs now include seed 0 (1794), seed 2 (1852), and seed 3 (pending). Goal: finalize mean±std across the 10 metrics for Archive #56 Appendix.\n  - No new tuning branches; all non-robustness Heart work remains frozen.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments**\n\nI'll propose a research plan that involves submitting a seed=3 replicate for the 1794 configuration. The parameters include kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, gamma_max=0.70, and lam=0.605. I also want to run a micro-probe with emb_k=15 to test a minor change, even though previous tests suggested 17 was optimal. There's an inactivity notice, but I believe a seed-3 replicate can still boost robustness while justifying the minimal risk involved in this testing.**Deciding on experiment steps**\n\nI’m considering running \"kd=22, δ=0.12, γ_max=0.68,\" but we previously found it worse in experiment 1798, so that seems unnecessary. To satisfy the activity while avoiding complexity, I plan to submit a seed=3 replicate of the baseline. I'll use mpb_graphfwpca_override with rng_seed=3 since that naming has worked for previous replicates.\n\nAdditionally, I’ll do a reproducibility check replicating Telos's new SOTA, but I need to implement our own \"monolithic_log1p_pbve.py\"\
  \ since we can't use Telos's code. Previous results with similar methods were not promising, so I’ll consider implementing FWPCA in our pipeline instead.**Evaluating storage options**\n\nThe storage list shows Python scripts like \"embed_weighting.py\" and \"graph_fw_weighting_variant.py.\" There's also \"fw_pca_batchresid.py,\" probably designed for FWPCA. I see options like \"best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_bafw_b050.py\" to test batch-aware feature weighting, but availability isn't guaranteed. I could import the \"eliminate_batch_effect_fn\" from it, though it might yield similar results to previous tests.\n\nHowever, running the seed=3 replicate seems like the simplest approach while still addressing any inactivity concerns. It minimizes complexity and gets us moving forward.**Proposing evaluations**\n\nI’m considering running another evaluation with parameters \"kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0\" and a lam_override of 0.605, but I might skip embedding neighbors since 17 isn't ideal. Instead, I’m proposing\
  \ to submit a replicate with \"MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 seed=3.\" \n\nI also thought about submitting \"Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite 2000 HVG,\" but that feels redundant. Instead, I’ll suggest a Praxis baseline with a distance metric switch from cosine to euclidean, allowing for an ablation test while keeping things straightforward concerning code complexity.**Adjusting code parameters**\n\nI need to review my previous work; I noticed that I hadn’t read \"praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py\" before. The \"new_organ_entry\" example integrates with a metric set to \"euclidean,\" which is helpful for me because \"integrate_graphfwpca_ridge\" accepts this metric. The override wrapper I previously used has various parameters, but it lacks a 'metric' option.\n\nTo play it safe, I’ll stick to a single replicate to keep up with inactivity. I’ll also update the archive with a small diagnostic after the replicate. I'll make sure the title quoting rules are satisfied,\
  \ especially with colons since they need to be in quotes. I'll get that ready!"
