  I''m considering writing a short script to compute mean and standard deviation from my EIDs list, which includes 1794, 1852, and 1887. I want to retrieve evaluation logs, but I can only access logs from finished evaluations. Luckily, both 1794 and 1852 are finished, so I can review and parse those metrics, although it will use tokens. I''m thinking of developing a "storage/praxis/robustness_agg.py" utility that runs in test mode to compute aggregated stats later. With a token budget of 101k used out of 270k, this approach seems manageable.**Planning an aggregator script**


