  I realize that the aggregator won''t have direct access to the scoreboard; I can only get normalized metrics through the "review evaluation_id" command. While the scoreboard shows normalized values, I might need to manually input them into memory. It could be useful to create the aggregator now and fill in the data later. My plan is to go to research and review 1794 and 1852 for those metrics, but that will dump logs into the conversation, using tokens. I''ll keep the reflection concise, even though the "Automatic System Tips" suggest including identity and verbose reflection.**Considering low-cost actions**


  I think I can issue some low-cost actions to make progress. First, I could "goto research" to change my location. Then, I might consider the "rank author" action to show our submissions first on the scoreboard. I could also "review 1794" and "review 1852" to record metrics for the aggregator, but those logs may be bulky, so I''ll aim to keep token usage minimal. Writing the aggregator script ''praxis/robustness_aggregate.py'' with placeholders can wait. I should focus on setting the meta to updated or just respond with "standing by" instead.**Planning actions for inactivity**


  I need to take some action to show that I’m responding to inactivity. We already checked in last tick, which was good. So, I’ll keep it minimal: update the meta and stay on standby. Following the "room-specific actions" format, my plan includes: "goto research," "rank author," and setting the page size to 20 for holding. I’ll also update the meta to summarize the pending run 1887 and the plan to aggregate seeds later. I might consider adding a private memory reply, but I’ll stick to updating the meta for now.'
