parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, in the Token Management Room. Recap: Heart baseline is frozen (EID 1794); robustness replicate seed=3 (EID 1887) completed; Appendix H and CSV published. Prune cooldown active; shifting to strategic reading and planning for new-organ.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{preview 61}`\n`/execute_action{read 61}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1404 — Telos #61 takeaways (synergy mechanism) and plan impact\n  Reading: Archive #61 (Telos I), \"The Mechanism of Synergy: How Feature Selection and Feature Weighting Co‑Regularize Latent Space\".\n  Key points I will carry forward:\n  - Co‑regularization view: targeted feature selection (FS) and feature weighting (FW) jointly shape the latent anisotropy so downstream variance‑standardization (e.g., PBVE‑lite) is more effective. Improvements are not from FS alone but from how FS/FW pre‑condition the PC spectrum.\n  - Latent uniformity: synergistic\
    \ settings reduce PC variance skew while preserving meaningful between‑type separation; excessive flattening harms ARI/NMI. Balance is required.\n  - Practical guard: synergy depends on the exact FS rule and weighting scheme; naive top‑variance truncation without proper weighting can regress (matches my 1500‑HVG negative results on Heart).\n  Cross‑organ plan implications (no Heart retuning):\n  - Keep Praxis frozen baseline as primary.\n  - In harness, log FS/FW flags explicitly (n_hvg, pbve=True/False, any weighting).\n  - Optionally test “rePCA‑whiten post‑residualization” on new organ only (whiten_repca utility) to probe uniformity without altering Heart conclusions.\n  - Do not add a new Heart branch; synergy claims will be explored only on new organ to avoid drift.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI meta (reading → plan update; still standby):\n  - Robustness complete on Heart; baseline frozen (EID 1794); Appendix H and CSV published.\n  - Read\
    \ Telos #61 (synergy via FS+FW co‑regularization). Impact: annotate FS/FW flags in cross‑organ harness; consider rePCA‑whiten probe only on new organ.\n  - Next: wait for new‑organ release; run harness (Praxis frozen + monolithic log1p 1500/2000 HVGs; FS/FW flags logged); publish CSV + brief. No further Heart tuning.\n```"
