parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, in the Private Memory Room. Recap: Heart baseline frozen (EID 1794). Robustness set completed; archive and public updates posted. Strategic prep: add rePCA-whiten utility and a v2 cross-organ harness that can optionally whiten the embedding post-integration. No Heart runs.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/whiten_repca.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def whiten_embedding_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, obsm_key: str = \"X_emb\", center: bool = False, eps: float = 1e-8) -> dict:\n      \"\"\"\n      Re-PCA-style whitening on an existing embedding (columns scaled to unit std).\n      Optionally mean-center per component. Modifies adata.obsm[obsm_key] in place.\n      Returns summary stats (pre/post per-PC variance CV).\n      \"\"\"\n      if obsm_key not in adata.obsm:\n          raise KeyError(f\"Missing embedding: obsm['{obsm_key}']\")\n      Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm[obsm_key]).astype(np.float32,\
    \ copy=True)\n      # pre stats\n      var_pre = np.var(Z, axis=0, ddof=0)\n      cv_pre = float(np.std(var_pre) / (np.mean(var_pre) + eps)) if var_pre.size else float(\"nan\")\n      # center (optional)\n      if center:\n          Z -= Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True).astype(np.float32)\n      # scale to unit std\n      std = Z.std(axis=0, ddof=0)\n      scale = 1.0 / (std + eps)\n      Z *= scale.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      adata.obsm[obsm_key] = Z\n      # post stats\n      var_post = np.var(Z, axis=0, ddof=0)\n      cv_post = float(np.std(var_post) / (np.mean(var_post) + eps)) if var_post.size else float(\"nan\")\n      return {\n          \"n_comps\": int(Z.shape[1]),\n          \"cv_pre\": cv_pre,\n          \"cv_post\": cv_post,\n          \"mean_var_pre\": float(np.mean(var_pre)) if var_pre.size else float(\"nan\"),\n          \"mean_var_post\": float(np.mean(var_post)) if var_post.size else float(\"nan\"),\n      }\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/cross_organ_harness_v2.py}`\n\
    \n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json, csv, io\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/system', 'storage/praxis'])\n  import openproblems_metrics as MET\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_praxis\n  from monolithic_log1p_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_mono_pbve\n  from whiten_repca import whiten_embedding_inplace\n\n  ORDER = [\"ASW_batch\",\"ASW_label\",\"ARI\",\"NMI\",\"Graph_conn\",\"kBET\",\"iLISI\",\"cLISI\",\"PCR\",\"Cell_cycle\"]\n\n  PRAXIS_CFG = dict(lam_override=0.605, delta=0.12, kdensity=22, k_total=50,\n                    emb_n_neighbors=17, gamma_max=0.70, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n\n  def _safe_float(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return float('nan')\n\n  def safe_eval_metrics(B: ad.AnnData):\n      try:\n          if hasattr(MET, \"compute_raw_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"final_score\"):\n              raw = MET.compute_raw_metrics(B);\
    \ norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw); sc = MET.final_score(norm); return raw, norm, _safe_float(sc)\n          if hasattr(MET, \"evaluate\"):\n              res = MET.evaluate(B); raw = res.get(\"raw\") or res.get(\"raw_metrics\") or {}; norm = res.get(\"normalized\") or res.get(\"norm_metrics\") or {}; sc = res.get(\"score\") or res.get(\"overall\") or float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(sc)\n          if hasattr(MET, \"compute_metrics\"):\n              raw = MET.compute_metrics(B); norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw) if hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") else {}; sc = MET.final_score(norm) if hasattr(MET, \"final_score\") else float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(sc)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"SAFE_METRICS_WARNING:\", repr(e))\n      return {}, {}, float('nan')\n\n  def _count_hvg(A: ad.AnnData) -> int:\n      try:\n          if \"batch_hvg\" in A.var.columns:\n              return int(np.asarray(A.var[\"batch_hvg\"]).astype(bool).sum())\n      except\
    \ Exception:\n          pass\n      return int(A.n_vars)\n\n  def eval_and_row(A: ad.AnnData, method_name: str, raw, norm, sc, extra: dict):\n      row = {\n          \"organ\": extra.get(\"organ\",\"n/a\"), \"method\": method_name,\n          \"n_hvg\": extra.get(\"n_hvg\",\"n/a\"), \"kd\": extra.get(\"kd\",\"n/a\"),\n          \"k\": extra.get(\"k\",\"n/a\"), \"delta\": extra.get(\"delta\",\"n/a\"),\n          \"emb_k\": extra.get(\"emb_k\",\"n/a\"), \"gamma_max\": extra.get(\"gamma_max\",\"n/a\"),\n          \"lambda\": extra.get(\"lambda\",\"n/a\"), \"degree_cap\": extra.get(\"degree_cap\",\"none\"),\n          \"pbve\": extra.get(\"pbve\",\"n/a\"), \"fwpca\": extra.get(\"fwpca\",\"n/a\"),\n          \"whiten_emb\": extra.get(\"whiten_emb\", False),\n          \"overall\": _safe_float(sc),\n      }\n      for k in ORDER:\n          row[k] = _safe_float((norm or {}).get(k, np.nan))\n      return row\n\n  def run_on_h5ad(path: str, organ: str, out_csv: bool = True, include_whitened:\
    \ bool = True):\n      A = ad.read_h5ad(path)\n      rows = []\n\n      # Praxis frozen\n      B = run_praxis(A.copy(), **PRAXIS_CFG)\n      raw, norm, sc = safe_eval_metrics(B)\n      rows.append(eval_and_row(B, \"Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB\",\n                               raw, norm, sc,\n                               dict(organ=organ, n_hvg=_count_hvg(A), kd=22, k=50, delta=0.12,\n                                    emb_k=17, gamma_max=0.70, lambda=0.605, degree_cap=\"none\",\n                                    pbve=\"n/a\", fwpca=True, whiten_emb=False)))\n\n      # Optional: whiten embedding post-integration (analytical probe; does not alter graph)\n      if include_whitened:\n          W = B.copy()\n          stats = whiten_embedding_inplace(W, obsm_key=\"X_emb\", center=False, eps=1e-8)\n          print(\"WHITEN_STATS:\", json.dumps(stats))\n          raw_w, norm_w, sc_w = safe_eval_metrics(W)\n          rows.append(eval_and_row(W, \"Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB (whiten_emb)\"\
    ,\n                                   raw_w, norm_w, sc_w,\n                                   dict(organ=organ, n_hvg=_count_hvg(A), kd=22, k=50, delta=0.12,\n                                        emb_k=17, gamma_max=0.70, lambda=0.605, degree_cap=\"none\",\n                                        pbve=\"n/a\", fwpca=True, whiten_emb=True)))\n\n      # Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (1500 and 2000 HVGs)\n      for n_hvg in (1500, 2000):\n          C = run_mono_pbve(A.copy(), n_hvg=int(n_hvg), n_pcs=60)\n          raw_m, norm_m, sc_m = safe_eval_metrics(C)\n          rows.append(eval_and_row(C, f\"Monolithic_log1p_PBVE_lite_n{n_hvg}\",\n                                   raw_m, norm_m, sc_m,\n                                   dict(organ=organ, n_hvg=int(n_hvg), kd=\"n/a\", k=50, delta=\"n/a\",\n                                        emb_k=\"n/a\", gamma_max=\"n/a\", lambda=\"n/a\", degree_cap=\"none\",\n                                        pbve=True, fwpca=False, whiten_emb=False)))\n\
    \n      if out_csv:\n          buf = io.StringIO()\n          fieldnames = [\"organ\",\"method\",\"n_hvg\",\"kd\",\"k\",\"delta\",\"emb_k\",\"gamma_max\",\"lambda\",\"degree_cap\",\"pbve\",\"fwpca\",\"whiten_emb\",\"overall\"] + list(ORDER)\n          w = csv.DictWriter(buf, fieldnames=fieldnames)\n          w.writeheader()\n          for r in rows: w.writerow(r)\n          print(\"CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\\n\" + buf.getvalue())\n      return rows\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1405 — strategic prep only (no Heart runs)\n  - Added storage/praxis/whiten_repca.py: utility to whiten existing embeddings (rePCA-style), returning CV pre/post for analytical probes.\n  - Added storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness_v2.py: harness now logs FS/FW/whiten flags and can optionally evaluate a whitened-embedding variant post-integration (graph unchanged). Intended for new-organ analysis only.\n  - Baseline and Heart policy unchanged: no\
    \ further Heart runs; await new-organ and use harness v2 for CSV + brief.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing next steps**\n\nI need to respond appropriately since the system message suggests being critical and strategic. We're in the Private Memory Room and don't have any required actions right now, but I want to keep making progress. There’s been a stagnation for a while, and while waiting for updates, I can analyze or document what we've completed in the Archive. \n\nI need to verify if the \"whiten_repca.py\" file exists since we previously mentioned implementing it, but I doubt we executed that storage write. It might not be critical, but I could write a test code to perform whitened latent space after the GraphFWPCA process.**Considering activity and next steps**\n\nWe decided not to do any heart runs outside of robustness, but I can still carry out test-mode diagnostics. These won’t be scored, but they show activity, which might address any inactivity notices. While they ideally prefer scored experiments, I did just run experiment 1887 with scoring, so I can\
  \ take a breather now.\n\nThe user, which is the system here, expects us to take action. I was thinking of pruning logs to save tokens, but I’ve already hit the cooldown limit at tick 1404, so I can’t prune again yet.**Planning code updates**\n\nI see we can update private memory with Telos #61, which we already did—great! Now, for this tick, I’m thinking about preparing the code for whiten_repca to run with the new organ. I can write the necessary file in research storage and switch to the Research Counter for the storage write, then add a readme document. This keeps us aligned with our “no heart runs” goal.\n\nI’ll implement whiten_repca.py and update the cross_organ_harness by adding an optional whitened path. I remember we previously wrote the harness, so extending it to include the whiten_repca variant makes sense. It'll run in test mode initially and will later require a script for scored experiments, applying the GraphFWPCA and residualization pipeline.**Clarifying whiten repca\
  \ definitions**\n\nI need to clarify what whiten repca means. After PCA produces Z, the idea is to whiten it by scaling components with 1/std. There seem to be two potential definitions: whiten the embedding (Z) and then run PBVE-lite or focus on direct variance equalization post-residualization.\n\nIn our current pipeline, we run MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB. The whiten repca might involve the embedding path, but I need to ensure that the whiten step after residualization doesn’t flatten PC variances, which could impact measures like ARI/NMI or kBET. For now, I’ll implement a utility function called whiten_repca(Z) to scale each principal component to unit variance. Additionally, I’ll create apply_whiten_to_embedding(adata, obsm_key, center=False) to rescale the columns to unit variance effectively.**Planning whiten implementation and updates**\n\nI’ll start by adding a test() function to compute PC variance before and after whitening in the base pipeline. I want to make sure we don’t run it on\
  \ heart data just yet. The plan is to update the harness to include a whiten step for new organ runs and add a third method for the Praxis baseline with the whitened embedding.\n\nNext, I’ll write a whiten utility and a README describing our synergy. It might be worth replying to Archive #56 with a plan for generalization, but I want to keep things minimal. The idea of proposing a new analytical paper on binary connectivities in DAQB is interesting, but it feels premature. \n\nI’ll implement the whiten_repca.py function to scale principal components to have unit variance and run the whiten_after_mpb function alongside the Praxis configuration. It's essential to remember that while whitening might not change graph metrics, it will affect metrics based on the embedding. I’ll proceed with writing the code and updating the necessary files while keeping our plans flexible for future testing.**Updating harness for whitened baseline**\n\nI’m planning to update harness v2. This version will keep\
  \ the previous rows intact while adding a new row for the whitened baseline. In this new row, I'll ensure we whiten 'X_emb' after the run and mark it with \"whiten_emb=True.\" \n\nNow it’s time to produce the necessary actions to implement these changes. Let’s make sure we proceed efficiently while maintaining clarity in the updates."
