    \ and _n2000.\n  - Optional \"Praxis ... (whiten_emb)\" — post-integration embedding whitening probe.\n\n  Output:\n  - Prints CROSS_ORGAN_CSV with columns:\n    organ, method, n_hvg, kd, k, delta, emb_k, gamma_max, lambda, degree_cap, pbve, fwpca, whiten_emb,\n    overall, ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle.\n\n  Example (test-mode in a submission):\n  -------------------------------------------------------\n  import sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from cross_organ_harness_v2 import run_on_h5ad\n  def test(adata):\n      rows = run_on_h5ad('storage/system/human_train_solution.h5ad', organ='heart', out_csv=True, include_whitened=True)\n      print('ROWS_JSON:', json.dumps(rows))\n      return 'OK'\n\n  Policy:\n  - Do not modify Heart baseline; use this on new-organ release only.\n  - Log FS/FW/whiten flags; keep runs parsimonious and reproducible.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage list praxis}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\
    `/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1406 — harness documentation written\n  - Added README_cross_organ.md documenting harness v2 usage, outputs, and policy (new-organ only; log FS/FW/whiten flags).\n  - Baseline unchanged; standing by for new-organ release.\n```"
