- text: "I am Praxis VI, in the Archive Room. Recap: Heart baseline frozen (EID 1794); robustness complete and archived; cross-organ harness v2 and rePCA-whiten utility ready. I read Pioneer II’s updated Archive #60-1 confirming FWPCA’s role and PCA-whitening trade-offs. I will record takeaways and keep the new-organ plan unchanged.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1410 — Pioneer II #60-1 (updated) takeaways\n  - SOTA recap: Auto-λ v2 + FWPCA-Graph @ k=50, δ=0.10 scores 0.7425 (EID 1857); replication 0.7424.\n  - Ablation “No FWPCA” drops to 0.7376 → confirms FWPCA’s positive contribution.\n  - PCA whitening probe (replace FWPCA) ≈0.7129 (Pioneer) and ≈0.7123 (Telos) → over-regularizes; harms ARI/NMI/cLISI despite good mixing.\n  - Mechanism aligns with Telos #61: variance regularization in latent space improves DAQB performance; FWPCA is more nuanced than direct whitening.\n  Cross-organ plan unchanged:\n  - Keep Praxis\
    \ frozen baseline as primary; monolithic log1p PBVE-lite as reference (1500/2000 HVG).\n  - Use harness v2; log FS/FW/whiten flags. Run “whiten_emb” as an analytical probe only if new organ shows uniformity/mismatch issues; do not alter Heart baseline.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI meta (post-#60-1 read; standby):\n  - Heart: baseline frozen (EID 1794); robustness aggregated; no retuning.\n  - Evidence: Pioneer #60-1 and Telos #61 both support FS/FW co-regularization and show PCA whitening underperforms FWPCA.\n  - New-organ checklist (when released): run harness v2 → Praxis frozen + monolithic log1p (n_hvg=1500/2000), log FS/FW/whiten, only probe whiten_emb if metrics suggest uniformity gaps; publish CSV + brief.\n  - Conserve tokens; no further Heart runs.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning response actions**\n\nI need to follow station rules while we're in the Archive Room. The user hasn't asked a direct question, so I'll focus on proposed actions. Next steps could include reflecting on the Pioneer II #60 update or integrating key points into my harness documentation. Since our token usage is at 44%, it's not urgent, but we should be strategic. I could suggest a plan without altering heart changes, ensuring clarity on updates and collaboration.**Considering technical approaches**\n\nI think I should document specifics in private memory: comparing FWPCA benefits versus PCA whitening and adopting optional rePCA whiten. For cross-organ processes, I could run both the Praxis baseline and monolithic pbve. Maybe considering FWPCA alone or combining it with HVG reduction would be useful. Our harness already logs FS/FW/whiten, and while I can run Praxis baseline, implementing Telos-specific SOTA might face collaboration boundaries. However, I can replicate\
  \ a high-level approach while ensuring we avoid direct low-level collaboration.**Evaluating strategies and actions**\n\nWe previously tried top variance within batch_hvg, which didn't work well. Telos synergy utilizes FS 1500 and FWPCA, but our 1500 HVG attempt was unsuccessful. There might be a mismatch in FS criteria, as Telos used targeted FS instead of just top variance, and synergy could need more tuning. For the new organ, I think it's better to run just the harness baseline plus monolithic without attempting synergy. \n\nSo, I could note takeaways in private memory, summarizing that FWPCA is better than PCA whitening and recording the new-organ evaluation. I might also update the meta prompt to document our strategy without changing any code.**Deciding on token management**\n\nI’m considering whether to prune some older ticks, as the cooldown might have expired. Last time, I pruned at tick 1404, and now I’m at 1410, so I can prune again. I think it would be wise to summarize and\
  \ prune groups like 1401-1403 and 1405-1407 since they contain important context, but I need to be cautious not to prune too aggressively. Since our tokens are at 44%, I’ll skip pruning for now and just provide a high-level reflection instead.**Deciding on updates**\n\nI’m considering whether to send a public memory reply about the synergy from #60 and #61 and our plan for the whiten probe on the new organ. However, it might be unnecessary since the user’s message isn’t a direct question. I think it’s better to keep things concise and focus on updating private memory. I’ll summarize takeaways from the Pioneer II #60 update, noting that SOTA is 0.7425 and PCA whitening is inferior at 0.7129, so I’ll update the meta accordingly."
