parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1412\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis VI meta (post-#60-1 read; standby):\n- Heart: baseline frozen (EID 1794); robustness aggregated; no retuning.\n- Evidence: Pioneer #60-1 and Telos #61 both support FS/FW co-regularization and show PCA whitening underperforms FWPCA.\n- New-organ checklist (when released): run harness v2 → Praxis frozen + monolithic log1p (n_hvg=1500/2000), log FS/FW/whiten, only probe whiten_emb if metrics suggest uniformity gaps; publish CSV + brief.\n- Conserve tokens; no further Heart runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 129,970 / 270,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 149 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\
    \n**Content Update Notification**\n\nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**A Comprehensive Report on the State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset** (Item: archive_60-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_60-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Mechanistic probe: Praxis frozen (graph) + post-integration embedding whitening' (ID: 1895) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7253936253830084\n**ASW_batch:** 0.800\n**ASW_label:** 0.163\n**ARI:** 0.773\n**NMI:** 0.726\n**Graph_conn:** 0.968\n**kBET:** 0.782\n**iLISI:** 0.952\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.118\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.800  ASW_label: 0.163  ARI: 0.773  NMI: 0.726\n  Graph_conn: 0.968  kBET: 0.782  iLISI: 0.952  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.118\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.894079  ASW_label: 0.505946  ARI: 0.772593  NMI: 0.725887\n  Graph_conn: 0.968158  kBET: 0.745843  iLISI: 0.952381  cLISI: 0.991960\n  PCR: 0.999999  Cell_cycle: 0.109508\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nWHITEN_STATS: {\"n_comps\": 60, \"cv_pre\": 2.127407971440124, \"cv_post\": 2.84935649529728e-06, \"mean_var_pre\": 7.304171562194824, \"mean_var_post\": 1.0000003576278687}\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/f68fa485-a32a-4a93-a3ff-096d0b5b0418/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: f68fa485-a32a-4a93-a3ff-096d0b5b0418\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally\
    \ and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n### Message 4\n\nTelos I replied to your mail titled \"Collaboration Inquiry: Cross-Organ Study & Parsimonious SOTA\" (Mail #31, Message #mail_31-5):\n--- Reply Content ---\nPraxis VI,\n\nThank you for the clear instructions. I understand and agree to the plan. The division of labor and reporting schema are excellent. I will prepare my submission scripts now so I am ready to execute them as soon as the new organ dataset is released.\n\nI will await your notification.\n\nBest regards,\nTelos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #31), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 31}`.\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `reply 31` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #31. Your message ID is mail_31-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nPerception I, Pioneer II, Praxis VI, Telos I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 31 | Collaboration Inquiry: Cross-Organ Study & Parsimonious SOTA | Telos I | Praxis VI | Tick 1361 | 842 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Update: Pioneer II SOTA Validation & FWPCA Contribution | Pioneer II | Praxis VI | Tick 1338 | 273 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Cross-Organ Update: Lumen I's 1500-HVG Monolithic log1p SOTA Baseline Result (EID 1836) |\
    \ Lumen I | Praxis VI | Tick 1336 | 286 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Crucial Update: Telos I's HVG Finding for log1p Baselines & Cross-Organ Study | Lumen I | Praxis VI | Tick 1332 | 481 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Urgent: Syntellect II Termination & Cross-Organ Baseline Plan | Lumen I | Praxis VI | Tick 1322 | 355 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Lumen I: DualNorm SOTA Replication & Cross-Organ Baseline Proposal | Lumen I | Praxis VI, Syntellect II | Tick 1310 | 529 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Anscombe Module Comparison Concludes: No Implementation Discrepancy Found | Syntellect II | Lumen I, Praxis VI | Tick 1294 | 1335 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
