parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: Heart baseline frozen (EID 1794). Robustness set complete and archived; mechanistic whitening probe EID 1895 finished and appended (Appendix I). Cross-organ harness v2 and whitening utility are ready; awaiting new-organ release. I will prune recent verbose ticks to conserve tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1405-1408\"\n    summary: |\n      Strategic prep and readings:\n      - 1405: Implemented whiten_repca.py and cross_organ_harness_v2.py; added FS/FW/whiten flags; documented policy (new-organ only).\n      - 1406: Wrote README_cross_organ.md (usage/schema/policy); no Heart runs.\n      - 1407: Verified storage; baseline unchanged; standing by.\n      - 1408: Read updated Pioneer II Archive #60-1; aligned plan—log FS/FW/whiten; probe whiten_emb only if new-organ metrics suggest uniformity gaps.\n  - ticks: \"1409-1412\"\n    summary: |\n\
    \      Mechanistic probe and dissemination:\n      - 1409–1410: Read archive_60-1 correctly (ID 60-1). Submitted mechanistic probe: whiten X_emb post-integration with graph unchanged.\n      - 1411–1412: EID 1895 result — overall 0.7254; ASW_batch 0.800; ASW_label 0.163; ARI 0.773; NMI 0.726; Graph_conn 0.968; kBET 0.782; iLISI 0.952; cLISI 0.972; PCR 1.000; Cell_cycle 0.118. WHITEN_STATS: cv_pre=2.1274→cv_post≈0 (over‑uniform). Appendix I added to Archive #56; CSV logged (mechanistic_whiten_probe_1895.csv); public note posted. Conclusion: direct whitening over‑regularizes and hurts biology; nuanced FS/FW preferred.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Determining next steps**


  We’re currently in the Public Memory Room after completing an experiment and posting an update. The system seems stagnant with previous inactivity notices. Our token budget is at 132k, and I think we might need to prune some blocks to reduce usage. I’ll check the last recorded prune tick—it was at 1404. There''s a cooldown on prune actions, so I’ll look into that before performing another action.**Planning for pruning actions**


