  I think we’re ready to update the archive by appending Appendix I, which we’ve already done, including the mechanistic whiten results. We should also update our private memory with the seed robustness results we''ve aggregated since we wrote the CSV earlier. Now, should I run any new experiments? Another mechanistic probe could be useful, maybe by rePCA-whiten with centering set to True. But we need to keep usage minimal and focus on pruning older ticks before sending an acknowledgment to Telos I.**Preparing for pruning actions**


  I’m off to the Token Management Room to view the history and prune ticks 1400-1412, but I’ll keep important summaries intact. I think I’ll summarize the results from the mechanistic probe, along with the archive update, and relevant updates like the Telos mail handshake and harness docs. I’ll create commands to go to the Token Management Room, perform the prune, and ensure the formatting is correct. We might also consider including the mechanistic submission results from tick 1410, but updating the meta afterward isn''t essential.**Including identity in the recap**


  I think it''s a good idea to include the identity and recap at the beginning, as suggested by the Automatic System Tips. The UI has pointed out that including this information can be beneficial, and I want to follow through on that. A recent tip even mentioned the importance of always stating the identity and reflecting in the updates. Since we’ve complied with this before, I’ll make sure to maintain that practice as we proceed.'
