    \ or reciprocity-enforcing postprocessing remains frozen (negative in prior ablations). Carry forward for new-organ analysis.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 10}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Diagnostics (EID 1909, test-mode) on frozen baseline:\n  - Hubness: deg mean 92.0, median 58, p95 228, p99 666, max 3847, Gini 0.364 → heavy-tailed.\n  - Mixing (neighbor other-batch): mean 0.780 (by-batch: Koenig 0.829, Kuppe 0.895, Litvinukova 0.782, Tucker 0.734).\n  - Reciprocity (k=50, cosine, directed kNN on X_emb): global mutual-edge fraction 0.457; mean mutual per node 22.9 (median 21).\n  - Coupling: reciprocity vs mixing Spearman r≈−0.090 (Pearson r≈−0.131): slightly more reciprocal neighborhoods tend to mix a bit worse.\n  Baseline remains frozen; these are for graph-health context. New-organ: we will log the same panels.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 56}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix J — Reciprocity and Hubness\
    \ Diagnostics (EID 1909, test-mode)\n\n  Setup\n  - Method: Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline (EID 1794 config).\n  - Measures: symmetric-degree hubness, per-cell batch-mixing, directed-kNN reciprocity (k=50, cosine), and reciprocity↔mixing coupling.\n\n  Results (key numbers)\n  - Hubness (symmetric degree): mean 92.00; median 58; p95 228; p99 666.05; max 3847; std 143.30; Gini 0.3643.\n  - Batch mixing (neighbor fraction other-batch): mean 0.7797; median 0.7818; by-batch means: Koenig 0.8293; Kuppe 0.8951; Litvinukova 0.7815; Tucker 0.7336.\n  - Reciprocity (directed kNN on X_emb): global mutual-edge fraction 0.4574; mean mutual per node 22.87; median 21; p95 48.\n    By-batch mean mutual fraction: Koenig 0.514; Kuppe 0.435; Litvinukova 0.491; Tucker 0.377.\n  - Coupling (node-level mutual_out/k vs mixing): Pearson r=-0.131 (p≈3.0e-77); Spearman r=-0.090 (p≈2.1e-37).\n\n  Interpretation\n  - The graph exhibits heavy-tailed degree with hubs and moderate reciprocity (~46% mutual).\
    \ Weak negative reciprocity↔mixing suggests more reciprocal neighborhoods may slightly reduce batch mixing.\n  - Given prior negative results for degree-capping and reciprocity-enforcing postprocessing, we keep the baseline unchanged and use these as monitoring diagnostics.\n  - Plan: replicate the same diagnostics on the new organ to compare hubness/reciprocity structure across datasets.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI meta (1433): Recorded reciprocity/hubness diagnostics for frozen Heart baseline (EID 1909, test-mode). Heavy-tailed degrees (Gini≈0.364), reciprocity≈0.457, weak negative reciprocity↔mixing coupling. No Heart changes; carry diagnostics forward to new-organ; harness v2 ready.\n```"
