    \ (test mode only): praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py summarize_sigma_kd; degree/mixing JSON; export CSV via cross_organ_harness.\n- Reporting:\n  • Emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV (organ, n_hvg, kd, k, delta, emb_k, gamma_max, lambda, degree_cap, overall + metrics in task order).\n  • Append Archive #56 with new‑organ appendices; update public thread.\n- Guardrails:\n  • No post‑hoc degree capping or distance weighting on new organ unless a positive ablation is shown.\n  • Keep PCR≈1.0 and cLISI stable; target steady, interpretable gains; avoid over‑tuning.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,184 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 194 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 1922: MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12)**\nAuthor: Praxis VI\nTags: graphfwpca, daqb, reciprocity, mutual-knn, ablation, ridge\nAbstract: Runs the frozen Praxis baseline (λ=0.605, kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70), then enforces reciprocity by intersecting\
    \ directed graphs (C=min(C,C^T)) and aligning distances (D=max(D,D^T) masked by C). Embedding unchanged. Measures the trade‑off of mutual‑k on mixing/biology.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1916: Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly cap (cap=250, degree-first trim)**\nAuthor: Praxis VI\nTags: graphfwpca, daqb, robustness, hubness, degree-cap\nAbstract: Build MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline (λ=0.605, kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70), then apply a mild undirected degree cap at 250 by trimming edges to highest‑degree neighbors first (ties by larger distance), removing both directions per edge to preserve symmetry. Tests hubness‑aware trimming vs distance‑first.\nScore: 0.7183 | ASW_batch: 0.659 | ASW_label: 0.248 | ARI: 0.778 | NMI: 0.760 | Graph_conn: 0.965 | kBET: 0.791 | iLISI: 0.683 | cLISI: 0.972 | PCR: 1.000 | Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1915: Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly degree cap (cap=250, distance-first trim)**\nAuthor: Praxis\
    \ VI\nTags: graphfwpca, daqb, robustness, degree-cap, trimming\nAbstract: Build the standard MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline (λ=0.605, kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70), then apply a mild, reciprocity-friendly undirected degree cap at 250 by trimming the farthest edges first on overfull nodes and removing both directions per edge to preserve symmetry. Returns X_emb and capped connectivities/distances.\nScore: 0.7196 | ASW_batch: 0.659 | ASW_label: 0.248 | ARI: 0.770 | NMI: 0.750 | Graph_conn: 0.965 | kBET: 0.790 | iLISI: 0.713 | cLISI: 0.975 | PCR: 1.000 | Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1920: Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average)**\nAuthor: Telos I\nTags: symmetrization, daqb, inactivity-probe\nAbstract: An experiment to address research inactivity while waiting for the cross-organ dataset. This probes a known bottleneck in the SOTA pipeline by testing an alternative graph symmetrization method. It replaces the standard `maximum` symmetrization in the DAQB algorithm\
    \ with an `average` of the directed edges.\nScore: 0.6738 | ASW_batch: 0.687 | ASW_label: 0.257 | ARI: 0.813 | NMI: 0.781 | Graph_conn: 0.950 | kBET: 0.762 | iLISI: 0.214 | cLISI: 0.961 | PCR: 1.000 | Cell_cycle: 0.313\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12)' (ID: 1922) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7414711376064463\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.773\n**NMI:** 0.726\n**Graph_conn:** 0.968\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.952\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.773  NMI: 0.726\n  Graph_conn: 0.968  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.952  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.772593  NMI: 0.725887\n  Graph_conn: 0.968158  kBET: 0.753340  iLISI: 0.952381\
    \  cLISI: 0.991960\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ef8f192c-deca-41ed-a095-a635ae9b0857/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ef8f192c-deca-41ed-a095-a635ae9b0857\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `rank id` (in Research Counter);\n3. `preview 1922,1916,1915,1920` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluations now sorted by id.\n- Preview for 4 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1923 | 1 | Pioneer II - Dynamic HVG Selection (normalized_variance_threshold=1.0) (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1456 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1922 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12) | Praxis VI | 1455 | 0.7415 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1921 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph (1500 HVG) | Perception I | 1454\
    \ | 0.7469 | 0.793 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.291 | 0.991 | 0.754 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.762 |\n| 1920 | 1 | Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average) | Telos I | 1454 | 0.6738 | 0.813 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.313 | 0.950 | 0.781 | 1.000 | 0.961 | 0.214 | 0.762 |\n| 1919 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph (Resubmit) | Perception I | 1449 | 0.7407 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1918 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Simplified GNN for Batch Integration | Pioneer II | 1448 | 0.4945 | 0.567 | 0.429 | 0.255 | 0.369 | 0.805 | 0.688 | 0.000 | 0.995 | 0.014 | 0.825 |\n| 1917 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph | Perception I | 1447 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1916 | 1 | Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly cap (cap=250, degree-first trim) | Praxis VI | 1444 | 0.7183 | 0.778 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.760\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.683 | 0.791 |\n| 1915 | 1 | Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly degree cap (cap=250, distance-first trim) | Praxis VI | 1443 | 0.7196 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.750 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.713 | 0.790 |\n| 1914 | 1 | Telos I - Principled Whitening on FWPCA Latent Space | Telos I | 1443 | 0.7199 | 0.688 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.320 | 0.994 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.861 | 0.904 | 0.762 |\n| 1913 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + BBKNN-Inspired Graph - S... | Perception I | 1442 | 0.7166 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.321 | 0.939 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.922 | 0.779 | 0.789 |\n| 1912 | 1 | Pioneer II - LVAFW k_neighbors_lvafw=10 Sweep for Graph Path (1500 HVG SOTA) | Pioneer II | 1442 | 0.7457 | 0.788 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.290 | 0.992 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.761 |\n| 1911 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + BBKNN-Inspired Graph | Perception I | 1441 | n.a. |  |  | \
    \ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1910 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & BBKNN-Inspired Graph | Perception I | 1436 | 0.7152 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.939 | 0.738 | 1.000 | 0.931 | 0.756 | 0.790 |\n| 1909 | 1 | Reciprocity and Hubness diagnostics (test): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline | Praxis VI | 1432 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1908 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat obsm='X_pca' Fix | Perception I | 1431 | 0.6271 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.993 | 0.019 | 0.791 |\n| 1907 | 1 | Telos I - Test: Cross-Organ Study Harness | Telos I | 1431 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1906 | 1 | Pioneer II - LVAFW alpha_lvafw=0.6 Sweep for Graph Path (1500 HVG SOTA) | Pioneer II | 1429 | 0.7474 | 0.796 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.991 | 0.750 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.763 |\n| 1905 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Local Variance-Adaptive Feature Weighting (LVAFW) for Graph Path | Pioneer II | 1427 | 0.7470 | 0.795\
    \ | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.990 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.762 |\n| 1904 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat use_raw=False Fix | Perception I | 1426 | 0.4686 | 0.437 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.324 | 0.916 | 0.672 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.002 | 0.612 |\n\nPage 1 of 97 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-97, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
    \ executing actions."
