role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1458\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis VI standby protocol (new-organ triggers):\n- Do not run new Heart experiments. Frozen baseline: MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB ridge (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70; EID 1794; PCR≈1.0).\n- When new organ releases:\n  1) Run praxis/new_organ_entry.py (ridge GraphFWPCA kd=22,k=50) with δ∈{0.10,0.12}, seed=0; then seed=1 confirm.\n  2) Run praxis/new_organ_pbve_entry.py (monolithic log1p → PCA60 → PBVE‑lite → kNN) as reference.\n  3) Optional: praxis/new_organ_dualnorm_entry.py (Anscombe‑emb + log1p‑graph) for parity check.\n  4) Equal‑quota probe: praxis/new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (kq=1280, k=50; cosine).\n  5) Diagnostics\
    \ (test mode only): praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py summarize_sigma_kd; degree/mixing JSON; export CSV via cross_organ_harness.\n- Reporting:\n  • Emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV (organ, n_hvg, kd, k, delta, emb_k, gamma_max, lambda, degree_cap, overall + metrics in task order).\n  • Append Archive #56 with new‑organ appendices; update public thread.\n- Guardrails:\n  • No post‑hoc degree capping or distance weighting on new organ unless a positive ablation is shown.\n  • Keep PCR≈1.0 and cLISI stable; target steady, interpretable gains; avoid over‑tuning.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 87,916 / 270,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 195 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1922**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12)\n**ID:** 1922\n**Tags:** graphfwpca, daqb, reciprocity, mutual-knn, ablation, ridge\n**Abstract:** Runs the frozen Praxis baseline (λ=0.605, kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12,\
    \ emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70), then enforces reciprocity by intersecting directed graphs (C=min(C,C^T)) and aligning distances (D=max(D,D^T) masked by C). Embedding unchanged. Measures the trade‑off of mutual‑k on mixing/biology.\n**Score:** 0.7414711376064463\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.773\n**NMI:** 0.726\n**Graph_conn:** 0.968\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.952\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.773  NMI: 0.726\n  Graph_conn: 0.968  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.952  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.772593  NMI: 0.725887\n  Graph_conn: 0.968158  kBET: 0.753340  iLISI: 0.952381  cLISI: 0.991960\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as\
    \ sp\nimport anndata as ad\n\nsys.path.extend(['storage', 'storage/praxis'])\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_base\n\nCFG = dict(\n    lam_override=0.605,\n    delta=0.12,\n    kdensity=22,\n    k_total=50,\n    emb_n_neighbors=17,\n    gamma_max=0.70,\n    cap=2.0,\n    rng_seed=0,\n)\n\ndef _to_csr(X):\n    if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n    if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\ndef _reciprocal_graph(C: sp.csr_matrix, D: sp.csr_matrix):\n    C = _to_csr(C).astype(np.float64)\n    D = _to_csr(D).astype(np.float64)\n    # Reciprocity: keep only edges present in both directions\n    C_rec = C.minimum(C.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    # Distances for reciprocal edges: use max of the two directed distances, masked by C_rec\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    D_rec = D_sym.multiply(C_rec).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    return C_rec, D_rec\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) ->\
    \ ad.AnnData:\n    A = run_base(adata, **CFG)\n    C = A.obsp['connectivities']\n    D = A.obsp['distances']\n    C_rec, D_rec = _reciprocal_graph(C, D)\n    A.obsp['connectivities'] = C_rec\n    A.obsp['distances'] = D_rec\n    # neighbors meta\n    A.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {'n_neighbors': int(C.shape[0] and 50), 'method': 'daqb+mutual', 'metric': 'cosine'}\n    }\n    return A\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ef8f192c-deca-41ed-a095-a635ae9b0857/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ef8f192c-deca-41ed-a095-a635ae9b0857\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\
