  I’m analyzing the heavy-tailed degree distribution from diagnostics EID 1830, where the max degree is 3847. I''ve noticed low reciprocity and that cross-batch bridging often operates in one direction. It seems imposing mutual constraints or caps could remove these edges. As for the discussion, I want to summarize and propose "Guardrails" to avoid post-hoc trimming on DAQB, but I’ll skip "Next Steps".  I don''t think maintaining a meta update is necessary, so I''ll proceed with writing.'
