role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  \"\"\"\n  Soft inbound-degree control during kNN construction (for DAQB-style graphs).\n\n  Idea:\n    - Build candidate neighbor pool (kq) per source i with distances d(i,j).\n    - Estimate node popularity pop[j] = how often j appears in candidate lists (proxy for inbound load).\n    - Adjust directed edge score by a soft penalty on target popularity:\n        score(i,j) = -distance(i,j) - alpha * log(1 + max(0, pop[j] - cap_in) / tau)\n    - Select top-k per source by adjusted score; optional equal-batch quota.\n    - Symmetrize with union (binary C = max(Cdir, Cdir.T)); distances D = min(Ddir, Ddir.T).\n\n  Notes:\n    - Not a post-hoc trim. Penalty is applied during selection, preserving strong one-direction bridges.\n    - Parameters: cap_in (~1.5–2.5×k),\
    \ tau (softness 20–40), alpha (0.1–0.2).\n  \"\"\"\n\n  def _softcap(x, cap_in=100.0, tau=30.0):\n      z = np.maximum(0.0, x - float(cap_in)) / max(1e-8, float(tau))\n      return np.log1p(z)\n\n  def knn_soft_inbound(\n      Z: np.ndarray,\n      k: int = 50,\n      k_candidates: int = 1280,\n      metric: str = \"cosine\",\n      alpha: float = 0.15,\n      cap_in: float = 100.0,\n      tau: float = 30.0,\n      batches=None,\n      equal_quota: bool = False,\n  ):\n      \"\"\"\n      Build symmetric kNN graph with soft inbound-degree control.\n      Returns:\n        C (csr,float64): binary connectivities (symmetric union)\n        D (csr,float64): distances (min over directions)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      kq = int(k_candidates)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=metric).fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_all = d_all[:, 1:]  # drop self\n      idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n      # Popularity proxy for\
    \ inbound load\n      pop = np.bincount(idx_all.ravel(), minlength=n).astype(np.float64)\n      pen = _softcap(pop, cap_in=cap_in, tau=tau) * float(alpha)\n\n      if equal_quota and batches is not None:\n          b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n          uniq = np.unique(b)\n          B = len(uniq)\n          per_batch_cap = max(1, int(np.ceil(k / max(1, B))))\n\n      rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          tgt = idx_all[i]\n          base = -d_all[i]\n          adj = base - pen[tgt]\n\n          if equal_quota and batches is not None:\n              used = {ub: 0 for ub in uniq}\n              order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")\n              sel = 0\n              taken = set()\n              for pos in order:\n                  j = int(tgt[pos])\n                  if j == i or j in taken:\n                      continue\n                  ub = b[j]\n                  if used[ub] < per_batch_cap:\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(j);\
    \ dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      used[ub] += 1; taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                      if sel >= k:\n                          break\n              if sel < k:\n                  for pos in order:\n                      j = int(tgt[pos])\n                      if j == i or j in taken:\n                          continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                      if sel >= k:\n                          break\n          else:\n              order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")[:k]\n              sel_idx = tgt[order]\n              rows.extend([i] * len(order))\n              cols.extend(sel_idx.tolist())\n              dists.extend(d_all[i, order].astype(float).tolist())\n\n      C_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(dists, dtype=np.float64),\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = C_dir.maximum(C_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D = D_dir.copy().minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      return C, D\n```"
