parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from graphfwpca_ridge import integrate_graphfwpca_ridge\n  from daqb_soft_inbound import knn_soft_inbound\n\n  # Ridge GraphFWPCA config (embedding via GraphFWPCA; we override graph with soft-inbound DAQB)\n  KD = 22\n  K = 50\n  N_PCS = 100\n  DELTA = 0.12\n  SEED = 0\n\n  # Soft inbound-degree control parameters\n  SOFT_CFG = dict(\n      k=K,\n      k_candidates=1280,\n      metric=\"cosine\",\n      alpha=0.15,     # penalty strength\n      cap_in=100.0,   # soft inbound cap (~2x K)\n      tau=30.0,       # softness\n      equal_quota=False,\n  )\n\n  def _degree_stats(C: sp.csr_matrix):\n      deg = np.asarray(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      if deg.size == 0:\n          return {\"n\": 0, \"mean\": 0.0, \"median\":\
    \ 0.0, \"min\": 0.0, \"max\": 0.0, \"std\": 0.0, \"p95\": 0.0, \"p99\": 0.0}\n      return {\n          \"n\": int(deg.size),\n          \"mean\": float(deg.mean()),\n          \"median\": float(np.median(deg)),\n          \"min\": float(deg.min()),\n          \"max\": float(deg.max()),\n          \"std\": float(deg.std()),\n          \"p95\": float(np.quantile(deg, 0.95)),\n          \"p99\": float(np.quantile(deg, 0.99)),\n      }\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # 1) Run ridge GraphFWPCA to obtain robust embedding (and initial graph, which we will override)\n      A = integrate_graphfwpca_ridge(\n          adata,\n          n_pcs=N_PCS,\n          k=K,\n          kd=KD,\n          delta=DELTA,\n          metric=\"euclidean\",\n          mutual_boost=1.10,\n          seed=SEED,\n      )\n\n      # 2) Build soft inbound-degree DAQB graph from embedding (preserve one-direction bridges)\n      Z = np.asarray(A.obsm['X_emb'])\n      batches =\
    \ np.asarray(A.obs['batch']).astype(str)\n      C, D = knn_soft_inbound(Z, batches=batches, **SOFT_CFG)\n\n      # 3) Attach graph and neighbors meta\n      A.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      A.obsp['distances'] = D\n      A.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': int(SOFT_CFG['k']), 'method': 'soft_inbound_daqb', 'metric': SOFT_CFG['metric']}\n      }\n\n      # 4) Minimal diagnostics to STDOUT\n      stats = _degree_stats(C)\n      print(\"NEW_ORGAN_SOFT_INBOUND_CFG:\", json.dumps({\"KD\": KD, \"K\": K, \"DELTA\": DELTA, \"SEED\": SEED, **SOFT_CFG}))\n      print(\"NEW_ORGAN_SOFT_INBOUND_DEGREE_JSON:\", json.dumps(stats))\n      return A\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1466 — Prepared new-organ soft-inbound entry:\n  - Wrote storage/praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py:\n    * Embedding via integrate_graphfwpca_ridge\
    \ (KD=22, K=50, Δ=0.12, N_PCS=100, seed=0).\n    * Graph replaced by soft inbound-degree DAQB (alpha=0.15, cap_in=100, tau=30, kq=1280, cosine).\n    * Emits degree JSON for quick sanity on new organ.\n  - Heart remains frozen (no scored soft-inbound runs). Await 1931 (test) diagnostics; apply on new organ only per guardrails.\n```\n\n"
