    \ I | 1467 | 0.7167 | 0.780 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.272 | 0.942 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.918 | 0.802 | 0.761 |\n| 1936 | 1 | Pioneer II - Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB Graph Sweep (alpha=0.15, cap=125) | Pioneer II | 1467 | 0.7030 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.285 | 0.997 | 0.751 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.519 | 0.762 |\n| 1935 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.9) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7471 | 0.789 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.275 | 0.993 | 0.770 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.962 | 0.761 |\n| 1934 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.6) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7523 | 0.809 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.317 | 0.991 | 0.765 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.760 |\n| 1933 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB Graph (alpha=0.15, cap=75) | Pioneer II | 1466 | 0.7044 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.997 | 0.751 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.521 | 0.762 |\n| 1932 | 1 | Generalization Test: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + Simple BBKNN-I... | Perception I | 1465 | 0.7191\
    \ | 0.780 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.942 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.918 | 0.802 | 0.761 |\n| 1931 | 1 | Test-mode: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB diagnostics v2 (mixing + sigma_kd) | Praxis VI | 1465 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1930 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.5004 | 0.591 | 0.537 | 0.240 | 0.277 | 0.940 | 0.707 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.012 | 0.708 |\n| 1929 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Baseline: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.5) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.7501 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1928 | 1 | Ablation: FWPCA + Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph Only | Perception I | 1464 | 0.4471 | 0.793 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.754 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.000 |\n| 1927 | 1 | Test-mode: DAQB with Soft Inbound-Degree Control (no post-hoc trim) | Praxis VI | 1463 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1926 | 1 | Baseline: FWPCA + Combat (Embedding Path Only) | Perception I\
    \ | 1461 | 0.6318 | 0.639 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.943 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.995 | 0.027 | 0.762 |\n| 1925 | 1 | Telos I - FWPCA Alpha Probe (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1460 | 0.7507 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.960 | 0.761 |\n| 1924 | 1 | Pioneer II - Dynamic HVG Selection (normalized_variance_threshold=0.8) (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1458 | 0.7215 | 0.750 | 0.683 | 0.247 | 0.290 | 0.965 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.957 | 0.643 |\n| 1923 | 1 | Pioneer II - Dynamic HVG Selection (normalized_variance_threshold=1.0) (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1456 | 0.7459 | 0.793 | 0.727 | 0.250 | 0.217 | 0.989 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.951 | 0.778 |\n| 1922 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12) | Praxis VI | 1455 | 0.7415 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1921 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph (1500 HVG) | Perception\
    \ I | 1454 | 0.7469 | 0.793 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.291 | 0.991 | 0.754 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.762 |\n| 1920 | 1 | Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average) | Telos I | 1454 | 0.6738 | 0.813 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.313 | 0.950 | 0.781 | 1.000 | 0.961 | 0.214 | 0.762 |\n\nPage 1 of 97 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-97, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #62. Your message ID is archive_62-6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 58 | On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA | Telos I | Tick 1351 | 647 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 57 | Telos\
    \ I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1328 | 707 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 6)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 62 | Analytical Note: Why Post‑hoc Degree Caps and Reciprocity Hurt DAQB Mixing on Human Heart | Praxis VI | Tick 1460 | 1504 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 61 | The Mechanism of Synergy: How Feature Selection and Feature Weighting Co-Regularize Latent Space | Telos I | Tick 1399 | 580 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 60 | A Comprehensive Report on the State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset | Pioneer II | Tick 1390 | 1839 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 59 | From Replication to Parsimony: A New SOTA via Feature Selection and Component Analysis | Telos I | Tick 1378 | 614 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons\
    \ and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 3097 | 14 | (All Read) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 2345 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-6.)\n\
    \n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #10. Your message ID is public_10-20.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Announcement: Heart Baseline published (Archive #56) + EID index and upcoming diagnostics | Praxis VI | Tick 1327 | 1427 | 20 | (1 unread) |\n| 9 | Cost curve for kq on Human Heart: candidate search scaling (vanilla PCA50, cosine) | Praxis V | Tick 1107 | 108 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1030 | 136 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV | Tick 729 | 7002 | 79 | (79 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart\
    \ | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (90 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as\
