tick: 1469
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 62}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — v3 (same-batch penalty) diagnostics: extreme over‑mixing\n\n  EID 1938 (penalty_scope='same_batch') results (test‑mode):\n  - DEGREE_JSON: mean 88.40, median 59, max 1700, std 98.33, p95 208, p99 506, gini 0.332 (heaviness reduced vs baseline gini 0.364, max 3847).\n  - MIXING_JSON (fraction other‑batch): all.mean 0.955 (per‑batch means 0.913–0.995), i.e., near‑complete cross‑batch neighbors.\n  - σ_kd summaries unchanged; coupling σ_kd↔mixing remains positive (Pearson≈0.231; Spearman≈0.239).\n  \n  Interpretation: penalizing only same‑batch popularity flips the failure mode — from under‑mixing (v2) to over‑mixing. A row‑aware balance is needed, not a global penalty. We will not score on Heart.\n  \n  Next design: add per‑row balanced quotas toward a target mixing rate (e.g., ~0.78 other‑batch for Heart), enforced during selection (no post‑hoc trim), combined with same‑batch popularity\
    \ penalty. Validate on new organs only.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  \"\"\"\n  Soft inbound-degree control during kNN selection for DAQB-style graphs.\n\n  Provided functions:\n    - knn_soft_inbound: global or same-batch-only popularity penalty (no row balance).\n    - knn_soft_inbound_balanced: same-batch penalty + per-row quotas toward target mixing.\n\n  Notes:\n    - All methods symmetrize with union (binary C=max(Cdir,Cdir.T)) and distances with min().\n    - These are NOT post-hoc trims; penalties/quotas are applied during selection.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  def _softcap(x, cap_in=100.0, tau=30.0):\n      z = np.maximum(0.0, x - float(cap_in)) / max(1e-8, float(tau))\n      return np.log1p(z)\n\n  def knn_soft_inbound(\n      Z: np.ndarray,\n      k: int = 50,\n      k_candidates: int =\
    \ 1280,\n      metric: str = \"cosine\",\n      alpha: float = 0.15,\n      cap_in: float = 100.0,\n      tau: float = 30.0,\n      batches=None,\n      equal_quota: bool = False,\n      penalty_scope: str = \"all\",  # 'all' | 'same_batch'\n  ):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=int(k_candidates) + 1, metric=metric).fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_all = d_all[:, 1:]\n      idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n      pop = np.bincount(idx_all.ravel(), minlength=n).astype(np.float64)\n      pen_global = _softcap(pop, cap_in=cap_in, tau=tau) * float(alpha)\n\n      b = None; uniq = None; b_codes = None\n      if batches is not None:\n          b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n          uniq = np.unique(b)\n          _, inv = np.unique(b, return_inverse=True)\n          b_codes = inv.astype(np.int32)\n\n      if penalty_scope not in (\"all\", \"same_batch\"):\n          raise ValueError(\"penalty_scope must be 'all' or\
    \ 'same_batch'\")\n      if penalty_scope == \"same_batch\" and batches is None:\n          raise ValueError(\"penalty_scope='same_batch' requires batches\")\n\n      rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          tgt = idx_all[i]\n          base = -d_all[i]\n          if penalty_scope == \"all\":\n              pen_row = pen_global[tgt]\n          else:\n              mask = (b_codes[tgt] == b_codes[i])\n              pen_row = pen_global[tgt] * mask\n          adj = base - pen_row\n\n          if equal_quota and b is not None:\n              per_batch_cap = max(1, int(np.ceil(k / max(1, len(uniq)))))\n              used = {ub: 0 for ub in uniq}\n              order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")\n              taken = set(); sel = 0\n              for pos in order:\n                  j = int(tgt[pos])\n                  if j == i or j in taken: continue\n                  ub = b[j]\n                  if used[ub] < per_batch_cap:\n                      rows.append(i);\
    \ cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      used[ub] += 1; taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                      if sel >= k: break\n              if sel < k:\n                  for pos in order:\n                      j = int(tgt[pos])\n                      if j == i or j in taken: continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                      if sel >= k: break\n          else:\n              order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")[:k]\n              sel_idx = tgt[order]\n              rows.extend([i] * len(order))\n              cols.extend(sel_idx.tolist())\n              dists.extend(d_all[i, order].astype(float).tolist())\n\n      C_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(dists, dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = C_dir.maximum(C_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n\
    \      D = D_dir.copy().minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      return C, D\n\n  def knn_soft_inbound_balanced(\n      Z: np.ndarray,\n      batches: np.ndarray,\n      k: int = 50,\n      k_candidates: int = 1280,\n      metric: str = \"cosine\",\n      alpha: float = 0.12,\n      cap_in: float = 100.0,\n      tau: float = 30.0,\n      target_mix: float = 0.78,  # desired fraction of other-batch neighbors\n  ):\n      \"\"\"\n      Row-aware balanced selection:\n        - Penalize inbound popularity only for same-batch edges.\n        - Enforce per-row quotas toward a target other-batch fraction.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b)\n      B = len(uniq)\n      # Per-row quota plan\n      same_quota = int(np.clip(round((1.0 - target_mix) * k), 0, k))\n      cross_total = k - same_quota\n      cross_quota_base = cross_total // max(1, B - 1)\n      cross_quota = {ub: cross_quota_base for ub in uniq}\n     \
    \ # same-batch key will be overridden per row\n\n      # kNN candidates + popularity\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=int(k_candidates) + 1, metric=metric).fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_all = d_all[:, 1:]; idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n      pop = np.bincount(idx_all.ravel(), minlength=n).astype(np.float64)\n      pen_global = _softcap(pop, cap_in=cap_in, tau=tau) * float(alpha)\n\n      # Batch codes for fast compares\n      _, inv = np.unique(b, return_inverse=True)\n      b_codes = inv.astype(np.int32)\n\n      rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          tgt = idx_all[i]; base = -d_all[i]\n          # penalties only for same-batch edges\n          mask_same = (b_codes[tgt] == b_codes[i])\n          pen_row = pen_global[tgt] * mask_same\n          adj = base - pen_row\n\n          # per-row quotas\n          same_cap = same_quota\n          cross_caps = cross_quota.copy()\n          del cross_caps[uniq[b_codes[i]]]\n\
    \n          order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")\n          taken = set(); sel = 0\n          used_same = 0\n          used_cross = {ub: 0 for ub in cross_caps.keys()}\n\n          # First pass: fill respecting per-batch quotas (same and cross)\n          for pos in order:\n              j = int(tgt[pos])\n              if j == i or j in taken: continue\n              bj = b[j]\n              if mask_same[pos]:\n                  if used_same < same_cap:\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      used_same += 1; taken.add(j); sel += 1\n              else:\n                  if used_cross[bj] < cross_caps[bj]:\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                      used_cross[bj] += 1; taken.add(j); sel += 1\n              if sel >= k: break\n\n          # Second pass: top-up by best remaining while keeping total <= k\n          if sel < k:\n         \
    \     for pos in order:\n                  j = int(tgt[pos])\n                  if j == i or j in taken: continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                  taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                  if sel >= k: break\n\n      C_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(dists, dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      C = C_dir.maximum(C_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D = D_dir.copy().minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      return C, D\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, json\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from graphfwpca_ridge import integrate_graphfwpca_ridge\n  from daqb_soft_inbound import knn_soft_inbound_balanced\n\n  KD\
    \ = 22\n  K = 50\n  N_PCS = 100\n  DELTA = 0.12\n  SEED = 0\n\n  # Balanced row-aware quotas with same-batch popularity penalty\n  SOFT_BALANCED_CFG = dict(\n      k=K,\n      k_candidates=1280,\n      metric=\"cosine\",\n      alpha=0.12,\n      cap_in=100.0,\n      tau=30.0,\n      target_mix=0.78,  # other-batch fraction target (row-wise)\n  )\n\n  def _degree_stats(C: sp.csr_matrix):\n      deg = np.asarray(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      if deg.size == 0:\n          return {\"n\": 0, \"mean\": 0.0, \"median\": 0.0, \"min\": 0.0, \"max\": 0.0, \"std\": 0.0, \"p95\": 0.0, \"p99\": 0.0}\n      return {\n          \"n\": int(deg.size),\n          \"mean\": float(deg.mean()),\n          \"median\": float(np.median(deg)),\n          \"min\": float(deg.min()),\n          \"max\": float(deg.max()),\n          \"std\": float(deg.std()),\n          \"p95\": float(np.quantile(deg, 0.95)),\n          \"p99\": float(np.quantile(deg, 0.99)),\n      }\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData)\
    \ -> ad.AnnData:\n      A = integrate_graphfwpca_ridge(\n          adata,\n          n_pcs=N_PCS, k=K, kd=KD, delta=DELTA,\n          metric=\"euclidean\", mutual_boost=1.10, seed=SEED,\n      )\n      Z = np.asarray(A.obsm['X_emb'])\n      batches = np.asarray(A.obs['batch']).astype(str)\n      C, D = knn_soft_inbound_balanced(Z, batches=batches, **SOFT_BALANCED_CFG)\n      A.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      A.obsp['distances'] = D\n      A.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': int(K), 'method': 'soft_inbound_daqb_balanced', 'metric': SOFT_BALANCED_CFG['metric']}\n      }\n      print(\"NEW_ORGAN_SOFT_INBOUND_BAL_CFG:\", json.dumps({\"KD\": KD, \"K\": K, \"DELTA\": DELTA, \"SEED\": SEED, **SOFT_BALANCED_CFG}))\n      print(\"NEW_ORGAN_SOFT_INBOUND_BAL_DEGREE_JSON:\", json.dumps(_degree_stats(C)))\n      return A\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1469 — v3 over-mixed; prepared balanced row-aware design:\n  - v3 (same-batch-only penalty) produced near-complete cross-batch mixing (mean 0.955), so also undesirable.\n  - Implemented knn_soft_inbound_balanced(): same-batch popularity penalty + per-row quotas toward target_mix≈0.78; no post-hoc trim.\n  - Updated new-organ entry to use the balanced variant (target_mix 0.78, alpha 0.12). Heart remains frozen; validate on new organ only.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating configuration limits**\n\nI need to note that the current configuration, with an alpha of 0.15 and cap_in at 100 with tau at 30, might be too strong. It risks suppressing same-batch edges too much and leads to favoring cross-batch edges instead. The heavy-tail degree returns show interest, but they're lower than the baseline. Since we're in test mode, we won't score yet. The next steps involve per-edge gating and balancing the mixing fraction while enforcing quotas to avoid extremes. The previous equal-quota branch had a poor PCR.**Adjusting neighbor selection**\n\nI remember that the earlier equal-quota method using ridge-residualized PCA produced an overall result of 0.5893 and a PCR of 0.0, which came from a different pipeline. Now, I think the equal-quota in neighbor selection might still work in this context. I propose the idea of setting equal_quota to True and determining a per-batch cap. If we want to maintain cross-batch mixing around the baseline\
  \ of 0.78, this setup should help avoid dominance by a single batch while enforcing the neighbor limits.**Exploring soft-bridge balancing**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing \"soft-bridge balancing,\" where the penalty adjusts based on per-row counts. As neighbors are added for a specific item, I can tweak the penalty for same-batch edges when their count exceeds a target, like 12, and also penalize external batches that go over target_x. This might be more complex, but I can propose a design and write some stub code. I'm considering keeping everything within \"test-mode\" acceptance. It seems I should update Archive #62 to summarize v3 results and reflect these changes in public memory.**Developing an improved algorithm**\n\nI’m gathering the plan to enhance the algorithm by setting the penalty_scope to 'same_batch' and enabling equal_quota. I want to introduce a 'target_mix' parameter to calculate the per-batch cap for same-batch edges. If we don't know other batches, we can still set\
  \ equal_quota to True. I need to update the daqb_soft_inbound code to accept target_mix and dynamic gating, or create a new function called knn_soft_inbound_balanced. I'll be sure to document everything in both private and public memory. We also want to summarize v3 results in Archive #62 and plan for updates.**Preparing for new code implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about testing in “test mode,” but since we've already done two tests, it might be best to refrain from any more Heart tests and focus on the new-organ code instead. I plan to write a new organ entry using penalty_scope='same_batch', equal_quota=True, and an optional target_mix parameter. \n\nI’ll outline the implementation of function knn_soft_inbound_balanced, which will compute candidate neighbors and popularity counts, while also setting per-batch quotas. I’ll update our memory logs accordingly, write the necessary code into the appropriate file, and ensure everything is clear for future reference."
