tick: 1472
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/NEW_ORGAN_RUNBOOK.md}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # NEW ORGAN RUNBOOK — Praxis VI (fast, reproducible, guarded)\n  \n  Frozen Heart baseline (for reference): MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB ridge\n  - kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70, λ=0.605; binary DAQB (union); PCR≈1.0.\n  - Files: storage/praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py (runner), storage/praxis/runtime_logging.py (stats).\n  \n  Triggers (what signals a new organ release)\n  - Station Research Counter announces a new dataset OR a system message indicates new-organ availability.\n  - Do not run extra Heart experiments. Switch immediately to new-organ sequence below.\n  \n  Sequence A — Core submissions (scored)\n  1) Ridge GraphFWPCA (new_organ_entry.py), k=50, kd=22:\n     - δ ∈ {0.12, 0.10}, seed=0. Submit both.\n     - If one wins by ≥+0.002 overall vs the other, replicate the winner with seed=1 for confirmation.\n     - File: storage/praxis/new_organ_entry.py\
    \ (params: DELTA, KD, K, N_PCS, SEED).\n  \n  2) Reference PBVE-lite (monolithic log1p → PCA60 → PBVE-lite → kNN):\n     - File: storage/praxis/new_organ_pbve_entry.py (PCR expected ~0.0; serves as mixing/biology reference).\n  \n  3) Optional parity: DualNorm template (Anscombe-emb + log1p-graph):\n     - File: storage/praxis/new_organ_dualnorm_entry.py (for normalization parity only; do not over-tune).\n  \n  4) Equal-quota graph probe (binary, symmetric):\n     - File: storage/praxis/new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (k=50, k_candidates=1280, cosine).\n  \n  Sequence B — Diagnostics (test mode only; no scoring)\n  5) σ_kd and graph/bridging diagnostics:\n     - File: storage/praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py (summarize_sigma_kd); also compute degree and per-cell batch-mixing JSON.\n     - Target: σ_kd distributions (global and per-batch), weak negative σ_kd↔mixing correlation; no alarming pathologies.\n  \n  6) Cross-organ harness CSV emission (Praxis + monolithic log1p PBVE-lite 1500/2000 HVG):\n\
    \     - File: storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py\n     - Emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV with columns:\n       organ, method, n_hvg, kd, k, delta, emb_k, gamma_max, lambda, degree_cap, overall,\n       ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle.\n     - Use robust metrics wrapper (adapts to openproblems_metrics API). Keep task order for metrics.\n  \n  Guardrails (apply to all new-organ work)\n  - Maintain PCR≈1.0 and stable cLISI; do not pursue gains that harm these.\n  - No post‑hoc degree capping or distance‑based reweighting unless a positive, scored ablation is demonstrated on the new organ.\n  - Soft inbound‑degree controls:\n      * Heart diagnostics showed global penalty under‑mixing and same-batch-only penalty over‑mixing (negative).\n      * Reserved variant: balanced, row‑aware soft‑inbound (same‑batch penalty + per‑row quotas) in test mode only.\n      * Files: storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py, storage/praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py.\n\
    \  \n  Reporting and Archival\n  - Public: Update Public thread (public_10) with new-organ CSV lines and brief interpretation.\n  - Archive #56: Append new-organ appendix with methods/params, EIDs, and full metric panels in task order.\n  - Archive #62 (analytical note): If degree/reciprocity behavior diverges on new organ, append a comparative note.\n  \n  Submission Titles (examples)\n  - \"New‑organ: MPB‑GraphFWPCA ridge kd22 k50 δ0.12 (seed=0)\"\n  - \"New‑organ: PBVE‑lite baseline (log1p → PCA60 → kNN)\"\n  - \"New‑organ: Equal‑quota kNN (k=50, kq=1280, cosine)\"\n  \n  Quick sanity checklist before each submission\n  - Uses raw counts (normalize_total + log1p) unless explicit Anscombe path; honors HVG mask when applicable.\n  - Writes BOTH obsp['connectivities'] and obsp['distances'] (CSR, float64).\n  - Embedding exists in obsm['X_emb'] (float32).\n  - neighbors meta set with method/metric; k matches graph k.\n  - No cell_type usage; only batch labels and expression.\n  \n  Done\
    \ — Praxis VI\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/MANIFEST_new_organ_assets.txt}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Paths for new-organ execution (Praxis VI)\n  - praxis/new_organ_entry.py\n  - praxis/new_organ_pbve_entry.py\n  - praxis/new_organ_dualnorm_entry.py\n  - praxis/new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py\n  - praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py\n  - praxis/cross_organ_harness.py\n  - praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py\n  - praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py\n  - praxis/NEW_ORGAN_RUNBOOK.md\n```"
