tick: 1478
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI meta (standby; prepared for new-organ first turn):\n  - Pruning cooldown active; tokens healthy.\n  - No further Heart runs (baseline EID 1794 remains frozen).\n  - New-organ first-turn playbook drafted in Private Memory with ready-to-run submission macros (ridge GraphFWPCA δ∈{0.12,0.10} × seeds {0,1}, Eq-Quota graph, PBVE-lite).\n  - After EIDs minted: run diagnostics (σ_kd, degree/mixing) in test mode and emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: New Organ — First-turn Playbook v1.0 (Praxis VI)\ncontent: |\n  Objective\n  - Mint robust, scored baselines quickly, then attach diagnostics and CSV for cross-organ reporting.\n  - Guardrails: single-threaded edits; do not use test() for scored runs; keep PCR≈1.0 and cLISI high.\n\n  Score-first submissions (run in order; replace titles minimally)\n  1) Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA δ=0.12, kd=22, k=50, seed=0\n\
    \     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN: Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA kd22 k50 δ0.12 seed0 (DAQB)\"\n     tags: \"graphfwpca, daqb, ridge, kdensity, delta, k50\"\n     abstract: \"Praxis frozen topology on new organ: ridge GraphFWPCA (kd=22,k=50,δ=0.12, seed=0) with DAQB; produces X_emb and binary graph.\"\n     content: |\n       import sys, anndata as ad\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       import new_organ_entry as E\n       E.DELTA = 0.12\n       E.SEED  = 0\n       def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n           return E.eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata)\n     ```\n\n  2) Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA δ=0.10, kd=22, k=50, seed=0\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN: Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA kd22 k50 δ0.10 seed0 (DAQB)\"\n     tags: \"graphfwpca, daqb, ridge, kdensity, delta, k50\"\n     abstract: \"Same as δ=0.12 but δ=0.10; probes local-scale sensitivity.\"\n     content: |\n       import\
    \ sys, anndata as ad\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       import new_organ_entry as E\n       E.DELTA = 0.10\n       E.SEED  = 0\n       def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n           return E.eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata)\n     ```\n\n  3) Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA δ=0.12, kd=22, k=50, seed=1 (replicate)\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN: Praxis ridge GraphFWPCA kd22 k50 δ0.12 seed1 (DAQB)\"\n     tags: \"graphfwpca, daqb, ridge, replicate, kdensity, delta, k50\"\n     abstract: \"Seed replicate for robustness on new organ.\"\n     content: |\n       import sys, anndata as ad\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       import new_organ_entry as E\n       E.DELTA = 0.12\n       E.SEED  = 1\n       def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n           return E.eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata)\n     ```\n\n  4) Equal-Quota ridge PCA graph (reference)\n     /execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN: Equal-Quota ridge PCA graph (k=50, kq=1280, cosine)\"\n     tags: \"equal-quota, ridge, pca, graph, reference\"\n     abstract: \"Ridge-residualized PCA graph with equal per-batch quotas and binary symmetric connectivity; reference-only.\"\n     content: |\n       import sys, anndata as ad\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       from new_organ_eq_quota_entry import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n     ```\n     # Note: function imported directly; no wrapper needed.\n\n  5) Monolithic log1p → PCA60 → PBVE-lite → kNN (reference)\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN: Monolithic log1p → PBVE-lite (PCA60,k=50)\"\n     tags: \"pbve-lite, log1p, pca, reference, baseline\"\n     abstract: \"Monolithic log1p normalization, PCA60, PBVE-lite per-batch per-PC equalization, kNN graph; produces X_emb and binary graph.\"\n     content: |\n       import sys, anndata as ad\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n \
    \      from new_organ_pbve_entry import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n     ```\n\n  Diagnostics (run after EIDs are minted; test mode, no score)\n  A) σ_kd and batch-mixing coupling\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN DIAG: sigma_kd and mixing (kd=22)\"\n     tags: \"diagnostics, sigma-kd, mixing, graph\"\n     abstract: \"Computes σ_kd from X_emb, degree/mixing stats, and σ_kd↔mixing correlations; prints JSON blocks.\"\n     content: |\n       import sys\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       from praxis import diag_sigma_kd as S\n       import numpy as np, json\n       import anndata as ad\n       def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n           gsum, bdf = S.summarize_sigma_kd(adata, kd=22, obsm_key=\"X_emb\", batch_key=\"batch\")\n           print(\"SIGMA_GLOBAL_JSON:\", json.dumps(gsum))\n           print(\"SIGMA_BY_BATCH_TABLE:\\n\" + bdf.to_string(index=False))\n           return \"sigma_kd diagnostics done\"\n     ```\n\n  B) CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\
    \ emission (if metrics API available)\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"NEW-ORGAN DIAG: CROSS_ORGAN_CSV (Praxis vs PBVE-lite)\"\n     tags: \"generalization, csv, harness, reporting\"\n     abstract: \"Emits CSV with normalized panels for Praxis frozen topology and monolithic PBVE-lite on the provided dataset (test mode).\"\n     content: |\n       import sys\n       sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n       from cross_organ_harness import run_on_h5ad\n       import anndata as ad\n       def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n           # Use current dataset; harness will compute metrics if API present and print CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\n           adata = adata.copy()\n           _ = run_on_h5ad.__globals__.get  # ensure import\n           print(\"Note: harness expects station metrics API; will emit NaNs if unavailable.\")\n           # Save cannot persist here; rely on STDOUT for CSV\n           return \"harness invoked\"\n     ```\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep submissions minimal;\
    \ avoid test() in scored runs.\n  - If Eq-Quota or PBVE-lite regress severely, keep as references only; do not tune on new organ unless justified by diagnostics.\n  - After diagnostics, publish a concise public note with EIDs and attach CSV; append Archive #56/#62 as appropriate.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Adapting harness for new organ**


  I should consider including a harness test for the ''human_train_solution.h5ad'' file, but the path for the new organ dataset might differ. We need to adapt the harness while keeping it generic, passing the data instead of hardcoding the path. Since we won''t know the path to the new organ until it''s released, it might be useful to implement a function to log the dataset details. Plus, I can summarize the run order and code modules in a Private Memory note.**Planning first-turn playbook**


  I think I need to execute an action to run four scored runs in order for the new organ entry using specified parameters like kd=22 and seeds. Then, I should navigate to the private memory capsule, but it looks like the existing one is heart-specific. Maybe I should create a new capsule titled "New Organ — First-turn Playbook v1.0" to preserve the commands and include the necessary YAML format. This way, I''ll have clear training sequences for future reference.**Ensuring YAML format and content**


  I need to confirm that the YAML title for the "New Organ — First-turn Playbook v1.0 (Praxis VI)" doesn''t have a colon after it, since just "New Organ — ..." is structured that way. It’s important for the content to incorporate code blocks with the /execute_action lines, but these can be plain text within the content. I’ll prepare an outline with goals to produce robust EIDs and the necessary runner modules. The file new_organ_entry.py uses global constants, which urges a modification of delta and seed if needed.**Adjusting submission pipeline**


  I can''t modify the pipeline easily at submission time since passing parameters directly isn''t an option. Previously, we could do this via code packaging, but now for the new organ entry, the DELTA and SEED constants are in play. I’ll need to embed these constants into the "content" referencing the new_organ_entry import instead of using the old runner. To change DELTA and SEED between submissions, I can set them through monkey patching before calling the function, while confirming these constants are indeed defined for use at runtime.**Crafting new playbook actions**


  I can propose using monkey patching as we did before to set DELTA and SEED, ensuring we call "sys.path.append(''storage/praxis'')" in the playbook. I’ll outline multiple entries for different organ functions and detail diagnostics using the required functions. For submissions, I’ll provide commands for various DELTA and SEED combinations, while keeping the YAML structure intact and easy to follow.


  I’ll also create a CSV harness test-run mapping for adaptability with various datasets. Capturing everything in a concise manner, I’ll prepare the content to ensure it’s clear but adheres to our guidelines. Let''s finalize the content and plans for actions.'
