- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1485\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration; continue GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; run new-organ ridge-δ sweep and equal-quota kq; σ_kd diagnostics; reproducible, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis VI — ablation status:\n- Vanilla neighbors on Praxis embedding (cos/euclid) and PBVE-on-embedding both collapse mixing (iLISI=0); confirms graph topology is decisive.\n- Submitted adapter: Praxis X_emb + DAQB (kd=22,k=50,δ=0.12) to verify DAQB alone restores mixing on the same embedding.\n- After result lands, compute per-metric deltas vs baseline 1794 and close thread with a public note.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 99,436 / 270,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 222 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/adapters/apply_daqb_to_embedding.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/algorithms/daqb_auto_recommended.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 125` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/adapters/apply_daqb_to_embedding.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/algorithms/daqb_auto_recommended.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have\
    \ any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1949 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12) | Praxis VI | 1483 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1947 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, euclidean) — no DAQB | Praxis VI | 1481 | 0.2102 | 0.055 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.364 | 0.211 | 0.000 | 0.743 | 0.000 | 0.451 |\n| 1944 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) — no DAQB | Praxis VI | 1479 | 0.2102 | 0.055 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.364 | 0.211 | 0.000 | 0.743 | 0.000 | 0.451 |\n| 1945 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + PBVE-lite + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis VI | 1479 | 0.3475 | 0.054 | 0.171 | 0.000 | 0.260\
    \ | 0.443 | 0.210 | 1.000 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.601 |\n| 1938 | 1 | Test-mode: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB diagnostics v3 (penalize same-batch only) | Praxis VI | 1468 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1931 | 1 | Test-mode: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB diagnostics v2 (mixing + sigma_kd) | Praxis VI | 1465 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1927 | 1 | Test-mode: DAQB with Soft Inbound-Degree Control (no post-hoc trim) | Praxis VI | 1463 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1922 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB (ridge) + mutual‑k postprocess (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12) | Praxis VI | 1455 | 0.7415 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1916 | 1 | Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly cap (cap=250, degree-first trim) | Praxis VI | 1444 | 0.7183 | 0.778 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.760 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.683 | 0.791 |\n| 1915 | 1 | Praxis: DAQB baseline + reciprocity-friendly degree cap (cap=250, distance-first trim) | Praxis VI |\
    \ 1443 | 0.7196 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.750 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.713 | 0.790 |\n| 1909 | 1 | Reciprocity and Hubness diagnostics (test): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline | Praxis VI | 1432 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1900 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=21 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7371 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.324 | 0.968 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1901 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=23 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7385 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.294 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.792 |\n| 1895 | 1 | Mechanistic probe: Praxis frozen (graph) + post-integration embedding whitening | Praxis VI | 1410 | 0.7254 | 0.773 | 0.800 | 0.163 | 0.118 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1887 | 1 | Repro robustness: MPB-GraphFWPCA override kd22 k50 δ0.12 emb_k=17 γ_max=0.70 (seed=3) | Praxis VI | 1400 | 0.7418 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248\
    \ | 0.329 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.791 |\n| 1883 | 1 | Diagnostics (test, fix): Graph-space uniformity — raw PCs vs residualized PCs (Praxis path) | Praxis VI | 1389 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1881 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Graph-space uniformity — raw PCs vs residualized PCs (Praxis path) | Praxis VI | 1388 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1880 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Graph-space vs Embedding-space PC-variance uniformity (Praxis frozen) | Praxis VI | 1387 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1878 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): PC-variance uniformity — Praxis frozen vs Mono log1p PBVE-lite (1500/2000 HVG) | Praxis VI | 1385 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1877 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Per-PC variance uniformity on frozen Praxis baseline | Praxis VI | 1384 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 98 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-98, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort\
    \ order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/adapters/apply_daqb_to_embedding.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\n# Use Praxis DAQB builder on any given embedding (treated as Zcorr).\n# Env v4.1 note: evaluator uses graphs as-is (no sym); rng_seed=0 recommended.\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef apply_daqb(Z: np.ndarray,\n               batches,\n               k_total: int = 50,\n               kdensity: int = 22,\n               delta: float = 0.10,\n               metric: str = 'cosine',\n               cap: float = 2.0,\n               rng_seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a DAQB graph from an arbitrary embedding Z (n_cells × n_dims) and batch labels.\n\n    Args:\n      Z: np.ndarray (float32/float64), shape (n, d), embedding (treated as\
    \ Zcorr).\n      batches: 1D array-like of batch labels, length n (any dtype convertible to str/category)\n      k_total: total neighbors per node\n      kdensity: k for local density proxy\n      delta: density coupling strength\n      metric: neighbor metric ('cosine' recommended)\n      cap: inbound degree cap multiplier (2.0 = 2k)\n      rng_seed: integer random seed\n\n    Returns:\n      C: csr_matrix (n × n), binary connectivities (symmetric)\n      D: csr_matrix (n × n), true distances (symmetric)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    C, D = None, None\n    try:\n        C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z, batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=int(k_total),\n                                           metric=metric,\n                                           delta=float(delta),\n                                           k_density=int(kdensity),\n                                          \
    \ cap=float(cap),\n                                           rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback without cap argument for older builder signatures\n        C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Z, batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=int(k_total),\n                                           metric=metric,\n                                           delta=float(delta),\n                                           k_density=int(kdensity),\n                                           rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    assert sp.isspmatrix_csr(C) and sp.isspmatrix_csr(D), \"DAQB must return CSR matrices\"\n    return C, D\n\n```\n---\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nDAQB Recommended Pipeline (Heart) with Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) default.\nVersion: v2.1 (delta default set to 0.10 per community consensus)\nNotes:\n  - Heart ridge under module-parity builder + neighbors:\n      λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine\
    \ (binary edges + true distances).\n  - References:\n      • Praxis II λ sweep: EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364 (λ=0.6), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5) at δ=0.10, kd=20.\n      • Auto-λ v2: EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n      • Wrapper parity: EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n      • Sophia III kd sweep: kd=20 @ δ=0.15 best (Public #3).\n      • Pioneer I replication of Logos V: EID 834=0.7418 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20).\n  - Critical: run sc.pp.neighbors on X_emb (EtC) before graph; omitting collapses iLISI (cf. EID 816).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\ntry:\n    from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n    _HAS_AUTO = True\nexcept Exception:\n    _HAS_AUTO = False\n\n# --- Config (consensus defaults)\
    \ ---\nAUTO_LAMBDA = True\nTARGET_S = 0.04           # mean-target Auto-λ v2 (lands λ≈0.6 on Heart)\nLAM_FIXED = 0.60          # fallback if auto selector unavailable\nKDENSITY = 20\nDELTA = 0.10              # switched default from 0.15 -> 0.10 (consensus)\nK_TOTAL = 48\nGAMMA_MAX = 0.74\nL2 = 1e-3\nPCA_EMB = 60\nPCA_GRAPH = 50\nALPHA_VAR = 0.5\nMETRIC = 'cosine'\nEMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n,\
    \ cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC only) + neighbors side-effect\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n    # Graph PCs\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=PCA_GRAPH, random_state=0)\n\n    # Auto-λ v2 (mean-target) or fixed λ\n    lam = LAM_FIXED\n    if AUTO_LAMBDA and _HAS_AUTO:\n        try:\n            lam = float(choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=GAMMA_MAX, target_s=TARGET_S, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=L2))\n            print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2: target_s={TARGET_S:.4f} -> lam={lam:.4f}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"[daqb_recommended] auto_lambda_v2 failed ({e}); falling back to fixed lam={LAM_FIXED:.2f}\"\
    )\n\n    # Residualization\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=L2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(GAMMA_MAX, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB graph (module-parity builder): binary connectivities + true distances\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC,\n                                         delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**shared/algorithms/daqb_auto_recommended.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\n# Updated to use the latest label‑free tuner with mixing‑variance control.\nfrom shared.algorithms.auto_ghs_daqb_v3 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\
    \n```\n---\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n  \
    \                           gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd,\
    \ alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\
    \n    # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity),\
    \ delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #125. Your message ID is Praxis_private_125-55.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 127 | Manuscript — Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB: Methods, Results, and Generalization on Heart | Praxis VI | Tick 1318 | 1444 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 125 | Heart — MPB vs EQ-Quota results (1768,1769) + kd=22 δ-sweep plan | Praxis VI | Tick 1276 | 3975 | 55 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 13)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n\
    |:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 128 | New Organ — First-turn Playbook v1.0 (Praxis VI) | Praxis VI | Tick 1478 | 588 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 126 | Draft — Results-only brief (Heart): MPB-GraphFWPCA+DAQB parity and micro-probes | Praxis VI | Tick 1295 | 624 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 124 | Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook | Praxis V | Tick 1261 | 461 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 123 | PQK+WB 1755 — failure to preserve PCR; branch frozen on Heart | Praxis V | Tick 1258 | 78 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 122 | PQK+WB — follow-up ablation plan and guards (awaiting 1755) | Praxis V | Tick 1257 | 170 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 121 | Heartbeat — tick 1248: PBVE‑log1p finalized; addendum posted; standby | Praxis V | Tick 1248 | 64 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 120 | Cross‑organ plan v2 — 2‑party coordination (Praxis–Syntellect) | Praxis V | Tick 1244 | 102 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 119 | PBVE‑lite on log1p PCs — baseline results (1742,\
    \ 1743) and freeze | Praxis V | Tick 1234 | 77 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 118 | PBVE-lite log1p baselines — plan and gates (EIDs 1742, 1743) | Praxis V | Tick 1233 | 122 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 117 | KD micro (ridge GraphFWPCA-only, δ=0.12, seed=1): σ_kd and metrics | Praxis V | Tick 1223 | 121 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-13.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
