tick: 1485
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12) — fixed import\"\ntags: \"embedding, daqb, adapter, graphfwpca, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Construct Praxis-style embedding (FWPCA-weighted PCA60), then apply DAQB via the shared adapter (apply_daqb) to test whether DAQB alone restores mixing on the same embedding.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  # Paths for shared adapter and praxis helpers\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/shared', 'storage/praxis'])\n\n  from adapters.apply_daqb_to_embedding import apply_daqb\n  from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  def _to_dense_float32(X):\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          return X.toarray().astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      return np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n \
    \     # Normalize from counts and log1p\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # Praxis-style FWPCA gene weights using batch labels\n      X = _to_dense_float32(adata.X)\n      y = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      f_scores, _ = f_classif(X, y)\n      finite = np.isfinite(f_scores)\n      max_finite = np.max(f_scores[finite]) if np.any(finite) else 1.0\n      f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=max_finite)\n      w = f_scores.astype(np.float32) / (np.mean(f_scores) + 1e-8)\n\n      # Embedding: PCA(60) on weighted expression\n      Xw = X * w[None, :]\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n\n \
    \     # DAQB on the embedding via shared adapter\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      C, D = apply_daqb(\n          X_emb, batches=batches,\n          k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.12,\n          metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n      )\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.astype(np.float64)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D.astype(np.float64)\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': 50, 'method': 'DAQB(adapter)', 'metric': 'cosine'}\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1485 — resubmitted adapter ablation with correct API:\n  - 1949 failed due to wrong symbol (wanted apply_daqb, not build_daqb_graph_from_embedding).\n  - Submitted corrected run: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (kd=22,k=50,δ=0.12) using shared.adapters.apply_daqb.\n  - Expectation:\
    \ iLISI and overall should recover toward frozen DAQB baseline on the same embedding, confirming graph construction is the driver.\n```"
