- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.10)\"\ntags: \"embedding, daqb, adapter, graphfwpca, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Same as δ=0.12 adapter ablation but with δ=0.10 to test local-scale sensitivity; verifies DAQB restores mixing on Praxis embedding across nearby δ.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/shared', 'storage/praxis'])\n  from adapters.apply_daqb_to_embedding import apply_daqb\n  from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n\n  def _to_dense_float32(X):\n      if sp.issparse(X):\n          return X.toarray().astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      return np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      X = _to_dense_float32(adata.X)\n      y = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      f_scores, _ = f_classif(X, y)\n      finite = np.isfinite(f_scores)\n      max_finite = np.max(f_scores[finite]) if np.any(finite) else 1.0\n      f_scores = np.nan_to_num(f_scores, nan=0.0, posinf=max_finite)\n      w = f_scores.astype(np.float32) / (np.mean(f_scores) + 1e-8)\n\n      Xw = X * w[None, :]\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n\n      C, D = apply_daqb(\n          X_emb, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\n          k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10,\n          metric='cosine', cap=2.0, rng_seed=0\n      )\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.astype(np.float64)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] =\
    \ D.astype(np.float64)\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': 50, 'method': 'DAQB(adapter)', 'metric': 'cosine'}\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis VI — awaiting adapter results:\n  - Running: 1951 (Praxis X_emb + DAQB, δ=0.12). Submitted: δ=0.10 variant to test sensitivity.\n  - Expectation: DAQB on Praxis embedding restores iLISI/mixing toward baseline (EID 1794) while PBVE-on-embedding and vanilla neighbors do not.\n  - When results land, compute per-metric deltas vs 1794 and post final ablation note; then return to standby for new-organ.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 125}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 1486 — queued δ=0.10 adapter control alongside δ=0.12:\n  - Purpose: confirm DAQB’s effect is robust across nearby δ on the same Praxis embedding.\n  - Pending:\
    \ 1951 (δ=0.12). New: δ=0.10 variant submitted.\n  - On completion: assemble Δ panels vs frozen baseline 1794 and close the graph-path ablation thread with a public summary.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning data retrieval and analysis**


  I’m thinking about retrieving the apply_daqb_to_embedding file content, which we''ve done before. For this tick, I can prepare a script to compute deltas once the evaluation results from result_human.h5ad are available. We could also consider pruning earlier ticks if token usage gets high, but at 106,790 out of 270,000 tokens, we’re okay for now. I don''t think a placeholder in Public Memory is necessary. I''ve also read the function docstring, so we''re all set for now!**Implementing metrics computation**


  I’m looking to implement a small script to postprocess results like obsm and graph connectivity stats, specifically to compute metrics every 10 inputs using openproblems_metrics. Earlier, we faced difficulties with system metrics, but for postprocessing, I think I can derive delta from the scoreboard instead of computing metrics. Unfortunately, there’s no API, so I’ll create code to run test() using system/human_train.h5ad to compute metrics with openproblems_metrics. The focus will be on integrating AnnData and relying on the results from 1951 for the metrics. I''ll set the meta update for that!**Preparing for log management and submissions**


  I’m considering our options for managing logs if token usage goes above the threshold, but for now, that doesn’t seem necessary. I could go to the Research Counter to set rank and page size, but that might not be required either. To add some value, I’m proposing another ablation with Praxis embedding and DAQB, using specific parameters for control. Since only one submission is running, I can submit a new control variant, δ=0.10, and check the code to ensure it uses apply_daqb properly. Then, I’ll craft a second submission for 1952.**Planning for submissions and updates**


  I’m outlining my actions: first, I’ll go to research to submit the δ=0.10 variant. I might consider adding the "apply_daqb" variant with kdensity and k_total. While updating Private Memory and structuring my submission similarly to previous ones, I can confirm it will use the same code. I think updating Public Memory isn’t necessary right now. I’ll also plan to summarize expectations in Private Memory, noting the confirmation criteria for both submissions. I’ll ensure proper YAML formatting and include ad.AnnData and sc.pp as needed!'
