parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 56}`\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Appendix N — Graph-topology ablations with Praxis embedding held fixed (EIDs 1944, 1947, 1945, 1951, 1953)\n\n  Goal\n  - Isolate the contribution of graph construction (neighbors vs DAQB) and embedding-space PBVE when the Praxis embedding is fixed.\n\n  Baseline (for reference)\n  - 1794 MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70): overall 0.7435; iLISI 0.952; cLISI 0.972; PCR 1.000.\n\n  Ablations (Praxis embedding held fixed)\n  - 1944 Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (cosine): overall 0.2102; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.743; PCR 0.000.\n  - 1947 Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (euclidean): overall 0.2102; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.743; PCR 0.000.\n  - 1945 Praxis X_emb + PBVE‑lite + neighbors (cosine): overall 0.3475; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.736; PCR 1.000.\n  - 1951 Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (δ=0.12): overall 0.2973; iLISI 0.940; cLISI 0.474; PCR 0.000.\n  - 1953 Praxis X_emb\
    \ + DAQB adapter (δ=0.10): overall 0.3024; iLISI 0.963; cLISI 0.497; PCR 0.000.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - DAQB alone restores cross‑batch mixing (iLISI ~0.94–0.96) but collapses biology and PCR without BRBG residualization.\n  - Vanilla neighbors (cos/euclid) and PBVE on the embedding cannot create cross‑batch edges (iLISI=0).\n  - The Praxis baseline’s strength is the synergy GraphFWPCA + BRBG (λ‑gated) + DAQB.\n\n  Artifact\n  - CSV (panels): storage/praxis/ablation_graph_topology_summary.csv\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1479-1487\"\n    summary: |\n      Graph-topology ablation thread (Praxis embedding fixed):\n      Baseline ref: 1794 (MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB kd=22,k=50,δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) → overall 0.7435; iLISI 0.952; cLISI 0.972; PCR 1.000.\n      Ablations:\n      - 1944 X_emb+neighbors (cosine): overall 0.2102; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.743; PCR 0.000.\n      - 1947 X_emb+neighbors\
    \ (euclidean): overall 0.2102; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.743; PCR 0.000.\n      - 1945 X_emb+PBVE‑lite+neighbors: overall 0.3475; iLISI 0.000; cLISI 0.736; PCR 1.000.\n      - 1951 X_emb+DAQB adapter δ=0.12: overall 0.2973; iLISI 0.940; cLISI 0.474; PCR 0.000.\n      - 1953 X_emb+DAQB adapter δ=0.10: overall 0.3024; iLISI 0.963; cLISI 0.497; PCR 0.000.\n      Notes: fixed adapter import (apply_daqb). Public summary posted; CSV saved at storage/praxis/ablation_graph_topology_summary.csv. Conclusion: DAQB is necessary but not sufficient; BRBG residualization is essential for preserving biology under DAQB. Thread closed; standby for new organ.\n```"
